{"total_count":30,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nikolife2016/pulsefeed-x402/issues/3","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nikolife2016/pulsefeed-x402","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nikolife2016/pulsefeed-x402/issues/3/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nikolife2016/pulsefeed-x402/issues/3/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nikolife2016/pulsefeed-x402/issues/3/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Nikolife2016/pulsefeed-x402/issues/3","id":5027968008,"node_id":"I_kwDOTQax-M8AAAABK7C0CA","number":3,"title":"radar: 47 веток ждут ответа","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11683768947,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTQax-M8AAAACuGgqcw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nikolife2016/pulsefeed-x402/labels/radar","name":"radar","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"Threads where our data answers the question","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":true,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":115,"created_at":"2026-07-31T08:41:56Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:06:59Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":"spam","sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Свежие вопросы, где у нас есть конкретный ответ — 2026-07-31 UTC\n\n- **[x402-foundation/x402#3006](https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/3006)** — [Feature]: Privacy-minimal receipt does not bind the payment terms of the accepted offer\n  чем полезны: схемы: в спеке их четыре, и у upto/auth-capture amount — потолок, а не цена; смена получателя и адреса-двойники — у нас есть история наблюдений\n- **[x402-foundation/x402#3005](https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/3005)** — [Feature]: Bazaar catalogs client-echoed service metadata without server-origin authentication\n  чем полезны: v2 переносит челлендж в заголовок PAYMENT-REQUIRED — тело перестало быть источником; проверка живости: npx x402-payable <url> покажет, где именно ломается\n- **[x402-foundation/x402#3004](https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/3004)** — [Feature]: auth-capture zero feeRecipient is a wildcard payout authorization that is easy to under-disclose\n  чем полезны: v2 переносит челлендж в заголовок PAYMENT-REQUIRED — тело перестало быть источником; проверка живости: npx x402-payable <url> покажет, где именно ломается\n- **[x402-foundation/x402#3003](https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/3003)** — [Feature]: Batch-settlement dynamic pricing permits receiver-authorized claims up to the payer-signed ceiling\n  чем полезны: v2 переносит челлендж в заголовок PAYMENT-REQUIRED — тело перестало быть источником; схемы: в спеке их четыре, и у upto/auth-capture amount — потолок, а не цена\n- **[x402-foundation/x402#3001](https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/3001)** — [Bug]: upto settlement amount is server-declared without protocol-verifiable usage\n  чем полезны: v2 переносит челлендж в заголовок PAYMENT-REQUIRED — тело перестало быть источником; схемы: в спеке их четыре, и у upto/auth-capture amount — потолок, а не цена\n- **[x402-foundation/x402#2997](https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/2997)** — CDP Bazaar: request delist/deactivate stale resource after endpoint stopped returning 402\n  чем полезны: v2 переносит челлендж в заголовок PAYMENT-REQUIRED — тело перестало быть источником; смена получателя и адреса-двойники — у нас есть история наблюдений\n- **[x402-foundation/x402#2993](https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/2993)** — Bazaar: a resource can be silently unpayable because its description is too long — document the limit and give\n  чем полезны: v2 переносит челлендж в заголовок PAYMENT-REQUIRED — тело перестало быть источником; проверка живости: npx x402-payable <url> покажет, где именно ломается\n- **[x402-foundation/x402#2978](https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/2978)** — Proposal: discovery extension — DNS + .well-known records for facilitator discovery\n  чем полезны: схемы: в спеке их четыре, и у upto/auth-capture amount — потолок, а не цена\n- **[14790897/MiQi#528](https://github.com/14790897/MiQi/issues/528)** — [BUG] API 402 Payment Required（余额不足）错误分类缺失，前端显示「内部错误」而非账单提示\n  чем полезны: проверка живости: npx x402-payable <url> покажет, где именно ломается\n- **[Merit-Systems/help-us#10](https://github.com/Merit-Systems/help-us/issues/10)** — StableEnrich: 403 Forbidden on POST /api/fullenrich/people-search (post-payment)\n  чем полезны: v2 переносит челлендж в заголовок PAYMENT-REQUIRED — тело перестало быть источником\n- **[Merit-Systems/x402scan#1045](https://github.com/Merit-Systems/x402scan/issues/1045)** — [Listing Request] code.mamenesia.com — Code Agent x402 v2 on Base (tip-jar $0.01)\n  чем полезны: v2 переносит челлендж в заголовок PAYMENT-REQUIRED — тело перестало быть источником\n- **[naMqe-h/onchain-agent#1](https://github.com/naMqe-h/onchain-agent/issues/1)** — Feature request: opt-in contract-risk context before EVM swap confirmation\n  чем полезны: v2 переносит челлендж в заголовок PAYMENT-REQUIRED — тело перестало быть источником\n\n_Ответ пишется вручную и от лица владельца. Радар только находит ветки; посты он не делает._","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nikolife2016/pulsefeed-x402/issues/3/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nikolife2016/pulsefeed-x402/issues/3/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/issues/21","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/issues/21/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/issues/21/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/issues/21/events","html_url":"https://github.com/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/pull/21","id":6018734592,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSuRVDc8AAAABKgcgQg","number":21,"title":"Add MCPSTG-SUPP-06: Test signed and publicly logged tool-manifest revisions","user":{"login":"intelligent-ears","id":186805503,"node_id":"U_kgDOCyJs_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186805503?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/intelligent-ears","html_url":"https://github.com/intelligent-ears","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/intelligent-ears/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/intelligent-ears/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/intelligent-ears/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/intelligent-ears/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/intelligent-ears/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/intelligent-ears/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/intelligent-ears/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/intelligent-ears/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/intelligent-ears/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2026-10-24T23:22:37Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T14:53:25Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/pulls/21","html_url":"https://github.com/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/pull/21","diff_url":"https://github.com/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/pull/21.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/pull/21.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## Gap\r\n\r\nSection 3.13 covers rug pulls well, but the tool-manifest pinning it describes ([What to snapshot](https://github.com/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/blob/main/03.%20MCP%20Threats%20and%20Attack%20Patterns/3.13-supply-chain.md#what-to-snapshot)) is local trust-on-first-use: each client hashes whatever `tools/list` returned the first time it connected. No test checks whether manifest revisions are signed by the expected publisher and recorded in a public, append-only transparency log.\r\n\r\nThat leaves three gaps:\r\n\r\n1. **First use is unverified.** If the server is malicious at first contact, the pin locks the malicious manifest in.\r\n2. **First use happens per machine.** Every laptop and CI runner pins separately, so a server can show the reviewer one manifest and a target another, and every local pin still passes. Only a shared log lets clients compare what they were served (split-view detection, as in Certificate Transparency).\r\n3. **A legitimate update looks the same as a rug pull.** A changed hash says something moved, not who published the new revision.\r\n\r\nThe local hash plus stop-and-ask in What to snapshot stays the baseline control (scored under SUPP-05 and TOOL-07). SUPP-06 proposes signed, logged revisions as an addition on top of it.\r\n\r\n## What changed\r\n\r\n- **New test `MCPSTG-SUPP-06`** (Medium, Hybrid), written in full to the `test-case-format.md` template. Six lab cases: an unsigned manifest at first use, a signed and logged revision (the positive control), a signed but unlogged revision, a revision from the wrong signer, a split view across two equally-authorized clients, and runtime drift with no new log entry. Three verdicts: Secure, Insecure (the client claims to verify and then accepts a bad envelope), and Not tested (no verifier, or the positive control fails). Includes a canonical-form procedure (RFC 8785 JCS + SHA-256), a synthetic envelope example (explicitly non-standard), and pseudocode for the admission check.\r\n- **New subsection** \"Local pins are trust-on-first-use\" under *Rug pulls and tool-description drift*.\r\n- **Provenance and signing:** a new mechanism-table row, plus a note that package provenance covers the package bytes but not the `tools/list` a remote server returns at runtime.\r\n- **Control matrix** row for malicious servers, rug pulls, and provenance. The drift list, test chains, and the 3.05 rug-pull `Tests:` line now reference SUPP-06.\r\n- **Appendix D:** placeholders `<TEST_USER_B>`, `<LAB_PUBLISHER_IDENTITY>`, `<LAB_OTHER_IDENTITY>`, `<LAB_TLOG>`.\r\n- **Appendix F:** a \"Transparency-log client\" tool category.\r\n- **Test count** updated from 79 to 80 in README, the chapter 3 overview, and `test-case-format.md`.\r\n- New references [30]–[33]: RFC 8785, RFC 9162, Sigstore Rekor, and SEP-3140 (closed 22 Sep 2026 without merge; may return through a working group).\r\n\r\n## Scope\r\n\r\nApplies to both local stdio and remote HTTP servers. Remote servers are the main case, because their `tools/list` can change without any package publish, so package provenance does not cover it. For local servers it matters when descriptions are generated at runtime or loaded from the network.\r\n\r\n## Severity\r\n\r\nMedium until a signing mechanism exists. The 2026-07-28 spec defines no signature, digest, or log field for tool definitions, and the MCP Registry does not record or sign them. A client without a manifest verifier is recorded as Not tested, not Insecure.\r\n\r\n## Review notes\r\n\r\n- All examples are synthetic and lab-only, using placeholders per `CONTRIBUTING.md`. The test explicitly says never to write lab entries to a public transparency log.\r\n- Mappings: OWASP MCP04:2025 (and MCP03:2025), CWE-347, CWE-494, and MITRE ATLAS AML.T0010.005. CWE-347 is used instead of CWE-345, which MITRE marks as Discouraged for mapping.\r\n- References to `MCPSTG-TOOL-07` are plain text until #19 lands. #16 and #19 also change the test count and the 3.05 `Tests:` line; I'll rebase after they merge.\r\n- SUPP-01 to SUPP-05 are still the generic template text. I've left them untouched here to keep this PR reviewable, and can follow up with separate PRs that make them concrete in the same style.\r\n\r\nAddresses the review request from @vermava.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/issues/21/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/issues/21/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/issues/3431","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/issues/3431/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/issues/3431/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/issues/3431/events","html_url":"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/issues/3431","id":5826753585,"node_id":"I_kwDOM2nIG88AAAABW000MQ","number":3431,"title":"Docs: quickstart MCP configs use unpinned `npx -y`, contradicting the Local Server Security guide","user":{"login":"basitalisandhu","id":62793038,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNzkzMDM4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62793038?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/basitalisandhu","html_url":"https://github.com/basitalisandhu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basitalisandhu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basitalisandhu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basitalisandhu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basitalisandhu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basitalisandhu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basitalisandhu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basitalisandhu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basitalisandhu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basitalisandhu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":24,"created_at":"2026-10-13T08:01:20Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T14:13:54Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### What's broken?\n\nThe documentation is wrong or misleading\n\n### Where in the spec or docs?\n\nhttps://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/develop/connect-local-servers and https://modelcontextprotocol.io/examples\n\n### What should happen?\n\nThe beginner examples should follow the [Local Server Security](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/tutorials/security/local-server-security) guide, which says to \"Install a specific version rather than `latest`\". For example `\"args\": [\"-y\", \"@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem@1.0.0\", ...]`, plus one sentence linking to that guide.\n\n### What actually happens?\n\nThe pages people copy from start every server unpinned: `docs/develop/connect-local-servers.mdx` (lines 100, 116, 216, 220, 273), `docs/examples.mdx` (lines 43, 50, 66 to 78), `docs/develop/build-client.mdx` (961) and `docs/tools/debugging.mdx` (131), in both the 2026-07-28 and draft versions. Each launch can fetch whatever was published last.\n\nThe pattern is widespread. In a random sample of 2,999 public GitHub repositories that ship agent skills or MCP configs, 159 of the 346 repositories that configure a local MCP server (46.0%) start at least one with no pinned version, and 63 of 346 (18.2%) ask for `latest` outright. A hand check found 19 of 22 findings correct. Caveat: it is a sample of what GitHub code search surfaces, not a census. Data and method: https://github.com/basitalisandhu/agent-skills-state-2026\n\n### Anything else?\n\nThe registry already rejects `latest` and version ranges for `server.json` packages (`internal/validators/validators.go`), so these docs are the main place that still teaches the unpinned form. If maintainers agree, I am happy to open the docs PR.\n\nAI disclosure: I used Claude Code to help prepare the analysis and draft this issue.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/issues/3431/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/issues/3431/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/argus/issues/18","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/argus","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/argus/issues/18/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/argus/issues/18/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/argus/issues/18/events","html_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/argus/pull/18","id":6308449313,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTCxG0M8AAAABOHxYug","number":18,"title":"chore(deps): bump the npm-minor-patch group across 1 directory with 11 updates","user":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12603398796,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTCxG0M8AAAAC7ziajA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/argus/labels/dependencies","name":"dependencies","color":"0366d6","default":false,"description":"Pull requests that update a dependency file","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12603398844,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTCxG0M8AAAAC7ziavA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/argus/labels/javascript","name":"javascript","color":"168700","default":false,"description":"Pull requests that update javascript code","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-10T14:05:04Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T14:05:09Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/argus/pulls/18","html_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/argus/pull/18","diff_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/argus/pull/18.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/argus/pull/18.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Bumps the npm-minor-patch group with 11 updates in the / directory:\n\n| Package | From | To |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [@modelcontextprotocol/sdk](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk) | `1.32.1` | `1.32.2` |\n| [@noble/post-quantum](https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum) | `0.6.1` | `0.7.1` |\n| [@x402/evm](https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402) | `2.28.0+aimarket.zod4.1` | `2.30.0` |\n| [@x402/fetch](https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402) | `2.28.0` | `2.30.0` |\n| [viem](https://github.com/wevm/viem) | `2.57.4` | `2.57.16` |\n| [@x402/core](https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402) | `2.28.0+aimarket.zod4.1` | `2.30.0` |\n| [@aimarket/agent](https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks) | `0.1.0` | `0.4.0` |\n| [@types/node](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/tree/HEAD/types/node) | `26.6.5` | `26.6.6` |\n| [@vitest/coverage-v8](https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/tree/HEAD/packages/coverage-v8) | `5.0.5` | `5.1.0` |\n| [tsx](https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx) | `4.22.4` | `4.23.15` |\n| [vitest](https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/tree/HEAD/packages/vitest) | `5.0.5` | `5.1.0` |\n\n\nUpdates `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` from 1.32.1 to 1.32.2\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/releases\">@​modelcontextprotocol/sdk's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>1.32.2</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>fix: add explicit | undefined to Transport optional properties (v1.x backport of <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/issues/1766\">#1766</a>) by <a href=\"https://github.com/kishormorol\"><code>@​kishormorol</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2814\">modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk#2814</a></li>\n<li>[v1.x] fix: allow registering after connect() when the capability was declared by <a href=\"https://github.com/claude\"><code>@​claude</code></a>[bot] in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2958\">modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk#2958</a></li>\n<li>chore: bump version to 1.32.2 by <a href=\"https://github.com/claude\"><code>@​claude</code></a>[bot] in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/3089\">modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk#3089</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>New Contributors</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/kishormorol\"><code>@​kishormorol</code></a> made their first contribution in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2814\">modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk#2814</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a href=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/compare/1.32.1...1.32.2\">https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/compare/1.32.1...1.32.2</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/3b73021a0a2272c0c04c3917bcdb03398b3ec63f\"><code>3b73021</code></a> chore: bump version to 1.32.2 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/issues/3089\">#3089</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/fa56d815aceceb089a695e765c98a83b8ce75421\"><code>fa56d81</code></a> [v1.x] fix: allow registering after connect() when the capability was declare...</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/6919e9526aa8bf4d31d4854e6deff1c2c80b7ed1\"><code>6919e95</code></a> fix: add explicit | undefined to Transport optional properties (v1.x backport...</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a href=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/compare/1.32.1...1.32.2\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `@noble/post-quantum` from 0.6.1 to 0.7.1\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/releases\">@​noble/post-quantum's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.7.1</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Added <code>@noble/post-quantum/webcrypto.js</code>, an async noble-style wrapper around the experimental built-in WebCrypto implementations of ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, ML-KEM-1024, and ML-KEM-768 + X25519. It supports deterministic raw-seed key generation, public-key derivation, encapsulation, decapsulation, and a memoized <code>isSupported()</code> probe that performs a complete round trip instead of checking method presence alone.</li>\n<li>Snapshot all options to ensure they're not mutated later</li>\n<li>Snapshot msg in <code>falcon*.attached.open()</code></li>\n<li>Ensure <code>falcon*.attached.open()</code> throws correct error for malformed sig / pubkey</li>\n<li><code>combineKEMS()</code> and <code>combineSigners()</code> now expect valid byte arrays</li>\n<li>Enforce digest lengths promised by pre-hash XOF OIDs: 32b for SHAKE128, 64b for SHAKE256</li>\n<li>Improve zeroization</li>\n<li>Improve Falcon signing and parsing: imported compact secret keys are rejected when the reconstructed sampler deviation is outside Falcon's proof interval</li>\n<li>Harden WebCrypto input validation</li>\n<li>Upgraded noble dependencies to 2.4.0</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Special thanks to Leon Acosta (from QuantaKrypto audits).</p>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/compare/0.7.0...0.7.1\">https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/compare/0.7.0...0.7.1</a></p>\n<h2>0.7.0</h2>\n<h3>Breaking</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><code>hybrid</code>: legacy aliases removed.</strong> <code>XWing</code>/<code>MLKEM768X25519</code> → <code>ml_kem768_x25519</code>, <code>MLKEM768P256</code> → <code>ml_kem768_p256</code>, <code>MLKEM1024P384</code> → <code>ml_kem1024_p384</code>, <code>QSFMLKEM768P256</code> → <code>QSF_ml_kem768_p256</code>, <code>QSFMLKEM1024P384</code> → <code>QSF_ml_kem1024_p384</code>, <code>KitchenSinkMLKEM768X25519</code> → <code>KitchenSink_ml_kem768_x25519</code>.</li>\n<li><strong><code>utils</code>: <code>afunction</code> no longer exported</strong> — moved to <code>@noble/curves/utils.js</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Other</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Falcon: Fix length check in detached (non-default) falcon</li>\n<li><strong><code>MultiplyNTTs</code> intermediate overflow</strong> — <code>a1*b1*zeta</code> could reach ~2³⁵; now <code>mod(mod(a1*b1)*zeta + a0*b0)</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>ML-DSA <code>sign</code> entropy ordering</strong> — randomness drawn before secret-key decoding, so an RNG throw can't leave partially-decoded key material live.</li>\n<li>ML-DSA <code>externalMu</code> length-checks <code>msg</code> as 64-byte µ; ML-KEM detaches the caller's public key before caching; <code>equalBytes</code> validates its inputs; stricter checks and messages throughout.</li>\n<li>Up to 2x speed boost for SLH-DSA</li>\n<li>+16-42% speed boost for hybrid ml-kem-768+x25519</li>\n<li>Upgrade noble deps to 2.3.0</li>\n<li>Reduce on-disk unpacked size, 813kb → 654kb (-159kb): by disabling source maps (they became less relevant).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/compare/2.2.0...2.3.0\">https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/compare/2.2.0...2.3.0</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">@​noble/post-quantum's changelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.7.1 (2026-08-27)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Added <code>@noble/post-quantum/gwebcrypto.js</code>, an async noble-style wrapper around the experimental built-in WebCrypto implementations of ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, ML-KEM-1024, and ML-KEM-768 + X25519. It supports deterministic raw-seed key generation, public-key derivation, encapsulation, decapsulation, and a memoized <code>isSupported()</code> probe that performs a complete round trip instead of checking method presence alone.</li>\n<li>Snapshot all options to ensure they're not mutated later</li>\n<li>Snapshot msg in <code>falcon*.attached.open()</code></li>\n<li>Ensure <code>falcon*.attached.open()</code> throws correct error for malformed sig / pubkey</li>\n<li><code>combineKEMS()</code> and <code>combineSigners()</code> now expect valid byte arrays</li>\n<li>Enforce digest lengths promised by pre-hash XOF OIDs: 32b for SHAKE128, 64b for SHAKE256</li>\n<li>Improve zeroization</li>\n<li>Improve Falcon signing and parsing: imported compact secret keys are rejected when the reconstructed sampler deviation is outside Falcon's proof interval</li>\n<li>Harden WebCrypto input validation</li>\n<li>Upgraded noble dependencies to 2.4.0</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Special thanks to Leon Acosta (from QuantaKrypto audits).</p>\n<h2>0.7.0 (2026-08-09)</h2>\n<h3>Breaking changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Removed legacy <code>hybrid</code> aliases:\n<ul>\n<li><code>XWing</code> and <code>MLKEM768X25519</code> → <code>ml_kem768_x25519</code>.</li>\n<li><code>MLKEM768P256</code> → <code>ml_kem768_p256</code>.</li>\n<li><code>MLKEM1024P384</code> → <code>ml_kem1024_p384</code>.</li>\n<li><code>QSFMLKEM768P256</code> → <code>QSF_ml_kem768_p256</code>.</li>\n<li><code>QSFMLKEM1024P384</code> → <code>QSF_ml_kem1024_p384</code>.</li>\n<li><code>KitchenSinkMLKEM768X25519</code> → <code>KitchenSink_ml_kem768_x25519</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Stopped exporting <code>afunction</code> from <code>utils</code>; it moved to <code>@noble/curves/utils.js</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Other changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fixed the length check in detached, non-default Falcon.</li>\n<li>Fixed an intermediate overflow in <code>MultiplyNTTs</code>, where <code>a1 * b1 * zeta</code> could reach approximately 2³⁵.</li>\n<li>Changed ML-DSA signing to draw entropy before decoding the secret key, so an RNG exception cannot leave partially decoded key material live.</li>\n<li>Made ML-DSA <code>externalMu</code> require a 64-byte <code>msg</code> value.</li>\n<li>Made ML-KEM detach the caller's public key before caching it.</li>\n<li>Made <code>equalBytes</code> validate its inputs and tightened other checks and error messages.</li>\n<li>Improved SLH-DSA performance by up to 2×.</li>\n<li>Improved hybrid ML-KEM-768 and X25519 performance by 16–42%.</li>\n<li>Upgraded noble dependencies to 2.3.0.</li>\n<li>Reduced unpacked package size from 813 KB to 654 KB by disabling source maps.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/commit/a23736036d4d5b34dd3a9e0ee312fd43d00154ac\"><code>a237360</code></a> Release 0.7.1.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/commit/89ddfa0c444ae24c2f184dcaaae97f5e35fea2c8\"><code>89ddfa0</code></a> Bump all deps</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/commit/20039f77e76f8e97ba281e0b9c0ec311f57e96cd\"><code>20039f7</code></a> Add changelog</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/commit/3b5f1982262ee210598d2a8a5f49ed6f7c7f0e2a\"><code>3b5f198</code></a> Bump ci workflows</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/commit/fbd31fdae922f4ec0db69c220fd80cdbc081f4e1\"><code>fbd31fd</code></a> Rename workflow</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/commit/07a8a15058e06cd7f125ca969d32d1be9d8f7842\"><code>07a8a15</code></a> Add fuzzing</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/commit/cf4cc8f7babca87566711c0624ac20f398e2be79\"><code>cf4cc8f</code></a> Fix tests</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/commit/4553bad3cb96164654b536754923291bf48acac8\"><code>4553bad</code></a> webcrypto: validate KEM outputs</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/commit/75626a26e81d75da441a3d6b15c9414230370a15\"><code>75626a2</code></a> hybrid: harden composition</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/commit/1942fa11c00c1a56cbe21bee3bfbd4e4ae9ef289\"><code>1942fa1</code></a> falcon: harden signature handling</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/compare/0.6.1...0.7.1\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `@x402/evm` from 2.28.0+aimarket.zod4.1 to 2.30.0\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/commit/3414a56618e94f5aeff1c03295f7d5879a56157a\"><code>3414a56</code></a> chore: version typescript packages  (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/4136\">#4136</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/commit/d95724bb7f4f81f52d20f9fba5f34b0c6ef0047f\"><code>d95724b</code></a> chore(go): release (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/4138\">#4138</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/commit/91806a3b6bb135f0e88c7d42b3174d3bcb9ad4d9\"><code>91806a3</code></a> chore: version python package  (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/4137\">#4137</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/commit/288400391ccd9dd7cc88f41eee8ad4234c6688a0\"><code>2884003</code></a> Pull request for mintlify/docs-update-1793816377937 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/4135\">#4135</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/commit/c349511f7336673bf38a2261533333bd7e01b3dd\"><code>c349511</code></a> feat(ts): facilitator-managed voucher custody for EVM batch settlement (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/4061\">#4061</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/commit/0f41a8dcc103feb2bc830a552307add305b407a8\"><code>0f41a8d</code></a> fix(core): use phase-specific error codes for throwing gate hooks (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/4133\">#4133</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/commit/7c9d6ad2acac1ca70f0ce0a1ac2560987ec56acb\"><code>7c9d6ad</code></a> fix(xrpl): enforce spend caps in issued-currency units (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/4110\">#4110</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/commit/8736fb7d8aefe2d6d07b72b3658feba520565084\"><code>8736fb7</code></a> Update docs/advanced-concepts/lifecycle-hooks.mdx (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/4132\">#4132</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/commit/29a81241fcb3d934d673b734dfc21e78341d860a\"><code>29a8124</code></a> fix(core): fail closed when a gate hook throws (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/3702\">#3702</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/commit/58e667ff091cfb9138c24a06c8f1ddd5546fc438\"><code>58e667f</code></a> fix(evm): return invalid_upto_evm_payload for malformed upto Permit2 payloads...</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/compare/npm-@x402/evm@v2.28.0...npm-@x402/evm@v2.30.0\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `@x402/fetch` from 2.28.0 to 2.30.0\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/commit/3414a56618e94f5aeff1c03295f7d5879a56157a\"><code>3414a56</code></a> chore: version typescript packages  (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/4136\">#4136</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/commit/d95724bb7f4f81f52d20f9fba5f34b0c6ef0047f\"><code>d95724b</code></a> chore(go): release (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/4138\">#4138</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/commit/91806a3b6bb135f0e88c7d42b3174d3bcb9ad4d9\"><code>91806a3</code></a> chore: version python package  (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/4137\">#4137</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/commit/288400391ccd9dd7cc88f41eee8ad4234c6688a0\"><code>2884003</code></a> Pull request for mintlify/docs-update-1793816377937 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/4135\">#4135</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/commit/c349511f7336673bf38a2261533333bd7e01b3dd\"><code>c349511</code></a> feat(ts): facilitator-managed voucher custody for EVM batch settlement (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/4061\">#4061</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/commit/0f41a8dcc103feb2bc830a552307add305b407a8\"><code>0f41a8d</code></a> fix(core): use phase-specific error codes for throwing gate hooks (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/4133\">#4133</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/commit/7c9d6ad2acac1ca70f0ce0a1ac2560987ec56acb\"><code>7c9d6ad</code></a> fix(xrpl): enforce spend caps in issued-currency units (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/4110\">#4110</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/commit/8736fb7d8aefe2d6d07b72b3658feba520565084\"><code>8736fb7</code></a> Update docs/advanced-concepts/lifecycle-hooks.mdx (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/4132\">#4132</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/commit/29a81241fcb3d934d673b734dfc21e78341d860a\"><code>29a8124</code></a> fix(core): fail closed when a gate hook throws (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/3702\">#3702</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/commit/58e667ff091cfb9138c24a06c8f1ddd5546fc438\"><code>58e667f</code></a> fix(evm): return invalid_upto_evm_payload for malformed upto Permit2 payloads...</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/compare/npm-@x402/fetch@v2.28.0...npm-@x402/fetch@v2.30.0\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `viem` from 2.57.4 to 2.57.16\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/releases\">viem's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>viem@2.57.16</h2>\n<h3>Patch Changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/wevm/viem/pull/5395\">#5395</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/c60ca26e030706610bcf61689331008a30a3db2a\"><code>c60ca26e030706610bcf61689331008a30a3db2a</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/jxom\"><code>@​jxom</code></a>! - <code>viem/tempo</code>: <code>gatewayActions</code> paid in the Gateway currency the Client account held most of, threw <code>Gateway.InsufficientFundsError</code> (with the account's balances) when it couldn't pay, and explained how to pay in <code>Gateway.PaymentRequiredError</code>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/wevm/viem/pull/5392\">#5392</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/9348d386a9f62fd6713124e25360d6040e4a34cf\"><code>9348d386a9f62fd6713124e25360d6040e4a34cf</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/gakonst\"><code>@​gakonst</code></a>! - Stopped retrying JSON-RPC method-not-found (<code>-32601</code>) and method-not-supported (<code>-32004</code>) errors from non-2xx HTTP responses, since a retry gets the same refusal.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/wevm/viem/pull/5392\">#5392</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/9348d386a9f62fd6713124e25360d6040e4a34cf\"><code>9348d386a9f62fd6713124e25360d6040e4a34cf</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/gakonst\"><code>@​gakonst</code></a>! - Reduced per-request overhead of the <code>http</code>, <code>webSocket</code> and <code>ipc</code> transports by building the <code>onFetchRequest</code> <code>Request</code> only when the hook is set and the <code>TimeoutError</code> only when a request times out, and fetched the withdrawal receipt once in the ZKsync <code>finalizeWithdrawal</code> and <code>isWithdrawalFinalized</code> actions.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/wevm/viem/pull/5392\">#5392</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/9348d386a9f62fd6713124e25360d6040e4a34cf\"><code>9348d386a9f62fd6713124e25360d6040e4a34cf</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/gakonst\"><code>@​gakonst</code></a>! - Cached signature hashes in <code>toSignatureHash</code>, so selector lookups in <code>decodeFunctionData</code>, <code>decodeEventLog</code>, <code>decodeErrorResult</code> and <code>encodeFunctionData</code> no longer hash every ABI item on each call.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/wevm/viem/pull/5391\">#5391</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/721d6824516514195c0a98971731c6d81b2f9032\"><code>721d6824516514195c0a98971731c6d81b2f9032</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/jxom\"><code>@​jxom</code></a>! - <code>viem/tempo</code>: Added experimental <code>Gateway</code> and <code>gatewayActions</code> (<code>client.ai</code>, <code>client.bucket</code>, <code>client.compute</code>, <code>client.kv</code>), with standalone <code>Actions.ai</code>, <code>Actions.bucket</code>, <code>Actions.compute</code>, and <code>Actions.kv</code>, with <code>client.gateway.getCapabilities</code>, <code>Actions.gateway.getCapabilities</code> and defaults for every option (<code>gatewayActions()</code>), for wallet-paid inference (including streamed text), object storage, metered and streamed CPU and GPU compute, and key-value state on a Tempo Gateway paid with a local Client account through the optional <code>mppx</code> peer dependency, with Tempo Wallet through the Accounts SDK, or with an app-supplied payment-aware <code>fetch</code>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>viem@2.57.15</h2>\n<h3>Patch Changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/wevm/viem/pull/5339\">#5339</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/a864b864b8b9031d970910fb8247471924d09280\"><code>a864b864b8b9031d970910fb8247471924d09280</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/mortezashojaei\"><code>@​mortezashojaei</code></a>! - Fixed <code>getAbiItem</code> to throw <code>AbiItemAmbiguityError</code> for overloads that JavaScript cannot distinguish, such as <code>bytes</code> vs <code>bytes32</code>, <code>uint256</code> vs <code>int256</code>, and <code>uint256[]</code> vs <code>uint256[2]</code>, while resolving distinguishable values by byte length and integer range.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/wevm/viem/pull/5321\">#5321</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/af062571382ec3631cf1901aeda9b58a87c8fad5\"><code>af062571382ec3631cf1901aeda9b58a87c8fad5</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/evanaronson\"><code>@​evanaronson</code></a>! - Removed a trailing slash to the ZKsync explorer URL.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/wevm/viem/pull/5358\">#5358</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/179a53682d9bf2ac2b7a65a86ec312fca0c7c9a8\"><code>179a53682d9bf2ac2b7a65a86ec312fca0c7c9a8</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/Turkchain1919\"><code>@​Turkchain1919</code></a>! - Added Turkchain Mainnet (Chain ID: 1919) to the supported chains.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/wevm/viem/pull/5375\">#5375</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/bb12b94649962cd7f03c339c226399c614b49805\"><code>bb12b94649962cd7f03c339c226399c614b49805</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/jxom\"><code>@​jxom</code></a>! - Fixed <code>decodeEventLog</code> and <code>parseEventLogs</code> to decode anonymous event logs when <code>eventName</code> names the event or every event in <code>abi</code> is anonymous, as with <code>getLogs</code> and <code>watchEvent</code> given a single anonymous <code>event</code>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/wevm/viem/pull/5364\">#5364</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/8f2a79ba8b4d235a24c4c101f4ef04a824c3e429\"><code>8f2a79ba8b4d235a24c4c101f4ef04a824c3e429</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/jxom\"><code>@​jxom</code></a>! - <strong>ccip:</strong> Applied the HTTP transport timeout (including its override) and 10 MiB response cap to CCIP-Read gateway requests, refused non-HTTP(S) gateway URLs (including <code>data:</code> URLs, which previously worked), and limited one lookup to 4 nested callbacks, 4 nested local batches, 256 gateway requests and 16 concurrent requests.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/wevm/viem/pull/5372\">#5372</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/f32ef6c41e623683b99989422eac7ac6cea5c107\"><code>f32ef6c41e623683b99989422eac7ac6cea5c107</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/jxom\"><code>@​jxom</code></a>! - Fixed <code>estimateGas</code> and <code>estimateContractGas</code> returning a gas limit filled by <code>eth_fillTransaction</code> that ignored <code>blockNumber</code>, <code>blockTag</code>, and <code>stateOverride</code>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/wevm/viem/pull/5360\">#5360</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/41801d827e339b96d1b4dd775f4dd379f17cc610\"><code>41801d827e339b96d1b4dd775f4dd379f17cc610</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/jxom\"><code>@​jxom</code></a>! - Raised the default expiring nonce <code>validBefore</code> from 25 to 270 seconds, capped <code>Relay.feePayer</code> expiring nonce windows at 300 seconds, added <code>Transaction.expiringNonceMaxExpiry</code>, and replaced the random expiring nonce <code>validAfter</code> with a random <code>nonce</code> discriminator.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/wevm/viem/pull/5360\">#5360</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/41801d827e339b96d1b4dd775f4dd379f17cc610\"><code>41801d827e339b96d1b4dd775f4dd379f17cc610</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/jxom\"><code>@​jxom</code></a>! - Fixed sponsored <code>prepareTransactionRequest</code> fills keeping a requested <code>feeToken</code> that the fee payer did not sign, which made the fee payer signature invalid.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/wevm/viem/pull/5378\">#5378</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/cbdd61078378012368464c9b0e4a76804a5ea987\"><code>cbdd61078378012368464c9b0e4a76804a5ea987</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/mmv08\"><code>@​mmv08</code></a>! - Fixed <code>fillTransaction</code> and <code>prepareTransactionRequest</code> returning <code>gasPrice</code> next to EIP-1559 fees on Anvil, which made <code>estimateGas</code> and <code>sendTransaction</code> fail on Anvil 1.8.5 and later with &quot;both gasPrice and (maxFeePerGas or maxPriorityFeePerGas) specified&quot;.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/wevm/viem/pull/5346\">#5346</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/7156f80f77c47c0a3f9df479b0a6e856029edb3b\"><code>7156f80f77c47c0a3f9df479b0a6e856029edb3b</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/KieranAltman\"><code>@​KieranAltman</code></a>! - Updated HashKey Chain and HashKey Chain Testnet display names, native currency name, and block explorer URLs.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/wevm/viem/pull/5373\">#5373</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/ddc2d365d093793f9d8f5818743f169c98eed8d7\"><code>ddc2d365d093793f9d8f5818743f169c98eed8d7</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/jxom\"><code>@​jxom</code></a>! - Added an optional <code>nonce</code> to <code>NonceManager</code> <code>reset</code> parameters, which <code>sendTransaction</code> and <code>sendTransactionSync</code> now set to the consumed nonce when a send fails after <code>consume</code> returned.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/wevm/viem/pull/5371\">#5371</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/035c519b6b6b3f179fa741953751a501f05132a2\"><code>035c519b6b6b3f179fa741953751a501f05132a2</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/jxom\"><code>@​jxom</code></a>! - Fixed <code>parseTransaction</code> to accept an EIP-7702 authorization <code>yParity</code> from 2 to 255 so a serialized transaction parses back, and made <code>recoverAuthorizationAddress</code> throw <code>InvalidYParityError</code> (and <code>verifyAuthorization</code> return <code>false</code>) for a <code>yParity</code> other than 0 or 1, which EIP-7702 treats as having no authority.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/wevm/viem/pull/5318\">#5318</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/57db085e896dfee3a3387fb7573bf7f7ebc6170d\"><code>57db085e896dfee3a3387fb7573bf7f7ebc6170d</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/jxom\"><code>@​jxom</code></a>! - Fixed <code>parseTransaction</code> not raising <code>TipAboveFeeCapError</code> when the encoded <code>maxFeePerGas</code> is zero.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/wevm/viem/pull/5377\">#5377</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/42c41ca3c42792e56a2e1f64d3007c28adc9fbba\"><code>42c41ca3c42792e56a2e1f64d3007c28adc9fbba</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/mmv08\"><code>@​mmv08</code></a>! - Fixed <code>sendTransactionSync</code> and <code>writeContractSync</code> failing at once and freeing the nonce when the node had accepted the transaction but stopped waiting for its receipt (<code>eth_sendRawTransactionSync</code> error code 4), even if the error had no transaction hash, and stopped <code>fallback</code> from sending that transaction to the next node.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/wevm/viem/pull/5388\">#5388</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/141f8c0ed7f5fdeafbfc514131781638e9340bd9\"><code>141f8c0ed7f5fdeafbfc514131781638e9340bd9</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/jxom\"><code>@​jxom</code></a>! - Added <code>Account.serialize</code> and <code>Account.deserialize</code> to <code>viem/tempo</code>, which store a configurable account (TIP-1107) as JSON and rebuild it with passkey owners that sign, and <code>Account.AddressMismatchError</code> for a version-zero config that does not derive the stored address. Added a <code>keyAuthorization</code> option to access key accounts, which attaches a signed key authorization to the account's transactions until the chain registers the access key.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/wevm/viem/pull/5318\">#5318</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/57db085e896dfee3a3387fb7573bf7f7ebc6170d\"><code>57db085e896dfee3a3387fb7573bf7f7ebc6170d</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/jxom\"><code>@​jxom</code></a>! - Fixed <code>maxPriorityFeePerGas</code> above a <code>maxFeePerGas</code> of <code>0n</code> not raising <code>TipAboveFeeCapError</code> or <code>MaxFeePerGasTooLowError</code> (including in actions that validate requests before calling the node, such as <code>call</code> and <code>estimateGas</code>), and fixed fee error messages dropping <code>0n</code> values.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/wevm/viem/pull/5370\">#5370</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/18b6b9041ef9d19421d182e6b0ca4b1caf5be09e\"><code>18b6b9041ef9d19421d182e6b0ca4b1caf5be09e</code></a> Thanks <a href=\"https://github.com/jxom\"><code>@​jxom</code></a>! - Fixed <code>validateTypedData</code> (and so <code>hashTypedData</code> and <code>signTypedData</code>) accepting field types that are not EIP-712 types, such as <code>uint7</code>, <code>uint264</code>, <code>uint08</code>, <code>int0</code> or <code>bytes0</code>, and field types that reference a struct missing from <code>types</code>, including in structs only referenced as array elements; it now throws <code>InvalidTypedDataTypeError</code>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/98aa491fda51f5a8f0b06dacffac8eb4c38ec171\"><code>98aa491</code></a> chore: raise <code>viem/ens</code> size limit (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/wevm/viem/issues/5398\">#5398</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/71241b2ba5dbfa510722c532ec072add3badc58f\"><code>71241b2</code></a> chore: version package (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/wevm/viem/issues/5393\">#5393</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/e1329c98c9a35e972edea0607abbd681cf8d66a1\"><code>e1329c9</code></a> fix(tempo): check Gateway chain and refresh balances before payment errors (#...</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/c60ca26e030706610bcf61689331008a30a3db2a\"><code>c60ca26</code></a> feat(tempo): fund-aware Gateway payments and InsufficientFundsError (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/wevm/viem/issues/5395\">#5395</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/264ab41da1db1b9585bde03582e569fe0686d419\"><code>264ab41</code></a> docs(tempo): use code groups with viem.config in Gateway guides (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/wevm/viem/issues/5394\">#5394</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/721d6824516514195c0a98971731c6d81b2f9032\"><code>721d682</code></a> feat(tempo): add experimental Gateway actions (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/wevm/viem/issues/5391\">#5391</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/9348d386a9f62fd6713124e25360d6040e4a34cf\"><code>9348d38</code></a> perf: skip retries for method refusals and trim per-request overhead (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/wevm/viem/issues/5392\">#5392</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/5711b7eb95292070b88b53b641498fe1f3a4a4a9\"><code>5711b7e</code></a> chore: version package (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/wevm/viem/issues/5363\">#5363</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/dbf8ae671d0f5e048480c6a6d80bfe5d2d87720f\"><code>dbf8ae6</code></a> test: stabilize <code>sendTransactionSync</code> timeout and <code>watchBlocks</code> catch-up test...</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/commit/141f8c0ed7f5fdeafbfc514131781638e9340bd9\"><code>141f8c0</code></a> feat(tempo): add Account.serialize, Account.deserialize and keyAuthorization ...</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a href=\"https://github.com/wevm/viem/compare/viem@2.57.4...viem@2.57.16\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `@x402/core` from 2.28.0+aimarket.zod4.1 to 2.30.0\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/commit/3414a56618e94f5aeff1c03295f7d5879a56157a\"><code>3414a56</code></a> chore: version typescript packages  (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/4136\">#4136</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/commit/d95724bb7f4f81f52d20f9fba5f34b0c6ef0047f\"><code>d95724b</code></a> chore(go): release (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/4138\">#4138</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/commit/91806a3b6bb135f0e88c7d42b3174d3bcb9ad4d9\"><code>91806a3</code></a> chore: version python package  (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/4137\">#4137</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/commit/288400391ccd9dd7cc88f41eee8ad4234c6688a0\"><code>2884003</code></a> Pull request for mintlify/docs-update-1793816377937 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/4135\">#4135</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/commit/c349511f7336673bf38a2261533333bd7e01b3dd\"><code>c349511</code></a> feat(ts): facilitator-managed voucher custody for EVM batch settlement (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/4061\">#4061</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/commit/0f41a8dcc103feb2bc830a552307add305b407a8\"><code>0f41a8d</code></a> fix(core): use phase-specific error codes for throwing gate hooks (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/4133\">#4133</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/commit/7c9d6ad2acac1ca70f0ce0a1ac2560987ec56acb\"><code>7c9d6ad</code></a> fix(xrpl): enforce spend caps in issued-currency units (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/4110\">#4110</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/commit/8736fb7d8aefe2d6d07b72b3658feba520565084\"><code>8736fb7</code></a> Update docs/advanced-concepts/lifecycle-hooks.mdx (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/4132\">#4132</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/commit/29a81241fcb3d934d673b734dfc21e78341d860a\"><code>29a8124</code></a> fix(core): fail closed when a gate hook throws (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/x402-foundation/x402/issues/3702\">#3702</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/commit/58e667ff091cfb9138c24a06c8f1ddd5546fc438\"><code>58e667f</code></a> fix(evm): return invalid_upto_evm_payload for malformed upto Permit2 payloads...</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a href=\"https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/compare/npm-@x402/core@v2.28.0...npm-@x402/core@v2.30.0\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `@aimarket/agent` from 0.1.0 to 0.4.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/releases\">@​aimarket/agent's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v0.4.0</h2>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/compare/v0.3.0...v0.4.0\">https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/compare/v0.3.0...v0.4.0</a></p>\n<h2>v0.3.0</h2>\n<p>Pays on production hubs with a credits key or a verified channel deposit.</p>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/compare/v0.2.2...v0.3.0\">https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/compare/v0.2.2...v0.3.0</a></p>\n<h2>v0.2.2</h2>\n<p>Strict Ed25519: a small-order key is refused. Published 0.2.1 still accepts a signature that verifies for every message under such a key.</p>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/compare/v0.2.1...v0.2.2\">https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/compare/v0.2.1...v0.2.2</a></p>\n<h2>v0.2.1</h2>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/commits/v0.2.1\">https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/commits/v0.2.1</a></p>\n<h2>v0.1.1</h2>\n<h1>aimarket-sdks v0.1.1</h1>\n<p>Release from the AICOM monorepo mirror (<code>main</code>), capturing changes since 2026-05-29.</p>\n<h2>Changes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>feat(aimarket): Pay-on-Verified settlement — Metis-gated escrow on paid invokes</li>\n<li>feat(ecosystem): THEOROS collab on landing, relay scout ops, fleet updates</li>\n<li>fix(security): full ecosystem audit — 43 verified findings across two passes</li>\n<li>fix(docs): point satellite markdown links at GitHub repos</li>\n<li>feat(oracles): 17-oracle family (6 new) + ARGUS conscience, live 3D previews</li>\n<li>fix(ops): VPS deploy hardening, Hub invoke gateway, and SDK/docs audit follow-ups</li>\n<li>feat(monitor): add ARGUS node; docs: 11 oracles everywhere</li>\n<li>docs+ops: trilingual SDK/ecosystem guides + LIVE-against-Base deploy + realistic UNI cadence</li>\n<li>fix(B): real vscode patch apply + SDK TEE pre-invoke verify + honest TEE test</li>\n<li>fix(sdks): unwrap hub channel envelope in TS/Dart/Rust (cohesion)</li>\n<li>cohesion: fix clear-cut ecosystem integrity findings</li>\n<li>security/quality: fix audit findings across the ecosystem</li>\n<li>feat(aimarket-sdks): ecosystem parity guard + registry publish readiness</li>\n<li>feat: standardize badges, CI coverage scripts, and docs across all satellites</li>\n<li>fix(aimarket-sdks): pad Ethereum wallet private key to 32 bytes in Dart</li>\n<li>feat(aimarket-sdks): production Ed25519 and EIP-712 crypto across Dart, TS, and Rust.</li>\n<li>fix: security audit — remove remaining 'plain words' references from bootstrap scripts and value.md headings</li>\n<li>Link all product READMEs to the public ecosystem landing page.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Source: monorepo path <code>aimarket-sdks</code> · <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks\">https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/commit/4d7d8b0efe2e993813cb75ca246347a50b00689c\"><code>4d7d8b0</code></a> chore(satellite): sync aimarket-sdks from aicom monorepo</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/commit/4ea5c42cc667f37cb9042b6c833a41e4856a52af\"><code>4ea5c42</code></a> chore(satellite): sync aimarket-sdks from aicom monorepo</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/commit/a5cfb89807eda430f350eeee5d14f1df4645d4d8\"><code>a5cfb89</code></a> chore(satellite): sync aimarket-sdks from aicom monorepo</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/commit/ce29a9b74dd287ffc123e1bf95505dc6d9715f48\"><code>ce29a9b</code></a> chore(satellite): sync aimarket-sdks from aicom monorepo</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/commit/d206cafa7aadeb8b8eafc9ae6473831d49d9e081\"><code>d206caf</code></a> chore(satellite): sync aimarket-sdks from aicom monorepo</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/commit/5d5b7d3e66b0e311f814b1dbd0ec985ceca395e9\"><code>5d5b7d3</code></a> chore(satellite): sync aimarket-sdks from aicom monorepo</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/commit/3981d93ff5c64787bba52892bff77724af1df3c4\"><code>3981d93</code></a> chore(satellite): sync aimarket-sdks from aicom monorepo</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/commit/12d340786d7488bac065ab68b3e26d42b27d1bc5\"><code>12d3407</code></a> chore(satellite): sync aimarket-sdks from aicom monorepo</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/commit/862d030f0cdc3eb2dad5a5376ec10f5667c2bd39\"><code>862d030</code></a> chore(satellite): sync aimarket-sdks from aicom monorepo</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/commit/e01fcf603053c887481ad2f891f0963829be0607\"><code>e01fcf6</code></a> chore(satellite): sync aimarket-sdks from aicom monorepo</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/compare/v0.1.0...v0.4.0\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `@types/node` from 26.6.5 to 26.6.6\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li>See full diff in <a href=\"https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/commits/HEAD/types/node\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `@vitest/coverage-v8` from 5.0.5 to 5.1.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/releases\">@​vitest/coverage-v8's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v5.1.0</h2>\n<h3>   🚀 Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add <code>--last-failed</code> to run only failed tests  -  by <a href=\"https://github.com/sheremet-va\"><code>@​sheremet-va</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/issues/11558\">vitest-dev/vitest#11558</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/commit/82f634220\"><!-- raw HTML omitted -->(82f63)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n<li>Support <code>Temporal.Instant</code> and <code>Temporal.ZonedDateTime</code> in <code>vi.setSystemTime()</code>  -  by <a href=\"https://github.com/Prajwal2246\"><code>@​Prajwal2246</code></a>, <strong>Prajwal2246</strong>, <strong>Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context)</strong>, <a href=\"https://github.com/hi-ogawa\"><code>@​hi-ogawa</code></a> and <strong>Codex (GPT-6)</strong> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/issues/11321\">vitest-dev/vitest#11321</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/commit/f150f5108\"><!-- raw HTML omitted -->(f150f)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n<li>Introduce <code>--since-last-run</code> flag  -  by <a href=\"https://github.com/sheremet-va\"><code>@​sheremet-va</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/issues/11516\">vitest-dev/vitest#11516</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/commit/08bd93b7e\"><!-- raw HTML omitted -->(08bd9)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n<li>Expose per-retry/repeat attempt result  -  by <a href=\"https://github.com/hi-ogawa\"><code>@​hi-ogawa</code></a>, <strong>Codex (GPT-6)</strong> and <strong>Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context)</strong> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/issues/11232\">vitest-dev/vitest#11232</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/commit/21be412ed\"><!-- raw HTML omitted -->(21be4)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n<li>Support fake timers for <code>node:timers</code> and <code>node:timers/promise</code>  -  by <a href=\"https://github.com/hi-ogawa\"><code>@​hi-ogawa</code></a>, <strong>OpenCode</strong> and <strong>Codex (GPT-6)</strong> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/issues/10899\">vitest-dev/vitest#10899</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/commit/fbe973cae\"><!-- raw HTML omitted -->(fbe97)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n<li>Allow coverage providers to store data in fs module cache  -  by <a href=\"https://github.com/AriPerkkio\"><code>@​AriPerkkio</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/issues/11747\">vitest-dev/vitest#11747</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/commit/54a2bdb81\"><!-- raw HTML omitted -->(54a2b)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n<li>Interactively review failed snapshots  -  by <a href=\"https://github.com/macarie\"><code>@​macarie</code></a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/hi-ogawa\"><code>@​hi-ogawa</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/issues/11325\">vitest-dev/vitest#11325</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/commit/54e5b8a8a\"><!-- raw HTML omitted -->(54e5b)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></li>\n<li><strong>browser</strong>:\n<ul>\n<li>Mock modules through an import map  -  by <a href=\"https://github.com/sheremet-va\"><code>@​sheremet-va</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/issues/11534\">vitest-dev/vitest#11534</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/commit/707f8adf4\"><!-- raw HTML omitted -->(707f8)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></a></