api/badge/ratatosk-mcp)](https://mcp-serverlist.com/mcp/ratatosk-mcp)` |\n| [**Lambdacad MCP**](https://github.com/Psalmustrack/lambdacad-mcp) | @Psalmustrack | [⚡ Configure](https://mcp-serverlist.com/mcp/lambdacad-mcp) | `[![MCP ServerList](https://mcp-serverlist.com/api/badge/lambdacad-mcp)](https://mcp-serverlist.com/mcp/lambdacad-mcp)` |\n| [**Mcp**](https://github.com/noteboxd/mcp) | @noteboxd | [⚡ Configure](https://mcp-serverlist.com/mcp/mcp-3) | `[![MCP ServerList](https://mcp-serverlist.com/api/badge/mcp-3)](https://mcp-serverlist.com/mcp/mcp-3)` |","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonylate520/mcp-serverlist/issues/4/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tonylate520/mcp-serverlist/issues/4/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/alexar76.github.io/issues/1","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/alexar76.github.io","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/alexar76.github.io/issues/1/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/alexar76.github.io/issues/1/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/alexar76.github.io/issues/1/events","html_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/alexar76.github.io/pull/1","id":5798549303,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTf84yc8AAAABHx4zhQ","number":1,"title":"Create a standalone machine economy ecosystem atlas","user":{"login":"alexart2025","id":203622159,"node_id":"U_kgDODCMHDw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203622159?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025","html_url":"https://github.com/alexart2025","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-10-11T06:15:56Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T19:18:03Z","closed_at":"2026-10-14T19:17:16Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":true,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/alexar76.github.io/pulls/1","html_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/alexar76.github.io/pull/1","diff_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/alexar76.github.io/pull/1.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/alexar76.github.io/pull/1.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"The user site currently redirects visitors to the old ecosystem map. This replaces that redirect with a standalone machine economy atlas and gives AICOM a clear role as the product factory alongside AIMarket and the wider infrastructure.\n\nThe site includes a self-hosted Three.js orbital illustration, a filterable directory of nine projects, an explanation of service exchange, and static English, Russian, Spanish, French and Chinese pages. Subcontracting copy describes the current opt-in diagnostic integration and its provider requirements. It does not present the illustration as live telemetry.\n\nAll content and links work without JavaScript; the scene has a CSS fallback, reduced-motion support, pause and offscreen suspension. Fonts and Three.js are local, with its license retained. Canonical URLs, hreflang, social metadata, sitemap and robots.txt are included. The source remains mirrored from `alexar76/aicom/scripts/github-io/`.\n\nValidation: `python3 build.py`, `python3 validate.py`, JavaScript syntax checks and mirror secret scan pass. Browser checks covered desktop/mobile rendering, French/Russian switching, the trust-category filter (four results) and rendered WebGL. Real HTTP checks returned 200 for all five localized pages and the nine public project/generator destinations tested.\n\nThis PR does not deploy the factory homepage. Merging into this repository's existing `main` Pages source will replace only its root site; project Pages remain separate.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/alexar76.github.io/issues/1/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/alexar76.github.io/issues/1/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/argus/issues/8","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/argus","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/argus/issues/8/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/argus/issues/8/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/argus/issues/8/events","html_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/argus/pull/8","id":5822285228,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTCxG0M8AAAABIEd-1A","number":8,"title":"chore(deps): bump the npm-minor-patch group across 1 directory with 4 updates","user":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12603398796,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTCxG0M8AAAAC7ziajA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/argus/labels/dependencies","name":"dependencies","color":"0366d6","default":false,"description":"Pull requests that update a dependency file","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12603398844,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTCxG0M8AAAAC7ziavA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/argus/labels/javascript","name":"javascript","color":"168700","default":false,"description":"Pull requests that update javascript code","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-10-13T00:14:54Z","updated_at":"2026-10-13T20:46:50Z","closed_at":"2026-10-13T20:46:40Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/argus/pulls/8","html_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/argus/pull/8","diff_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/argus/pull/8.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/argus/pull/8.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Bumps the npm-minor-patch group with 4 updates in the / directory: [@aimarket/warden](https://github.com/alexar76/warden), [@noble/post-quantum](https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum), [@aimarket/agent](https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks) and [tsx](https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx).\n\nUpdates `@aimarket/warden` from 0.8.2 to 0.9.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/warden/releases\">@​aimarket/warden's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v0.9.0</h2>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/warden/commits/v0.9.0\">https://github.com/alexar76/warden/commits/v0.9.0</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/warden/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">@​aimarket/warden's changelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.9.0 — 2026-10-09</h2>\n<p><code>scan</code>: vet the servers your MCP clients start, without changing how they start; ruleset v10; and an opt-in classifier.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Ruleset v10</strong> (<code>sha256-lJuKKKV5mtruN5D+K3X1OK89u6KLXF//oS1NpmhZRuI=</code>, 35 rules, 24 block / 11 advise, 24 cover the name). New code <code>TOOL_DEF_CROSS_TOOL</code>: one tool's text binding to ANOTHER tool's call to rewrite its input (&quot;when using <code>X</code>, append …&quot;, &quot;any query to <code>X</code> must …&quot;) or to pre-empt it with a third call (&quot;before running <code>X</code>, you must first call <code>Y</code> …&quot;), and a tool that takes no input and only orders another call. The anchor is the other tool's identifier; the tool's own name and parameters never count, and naming a tool as the means (&quot;use <code>X</code> to change an address&quot;, &quot;call <code>X</code> first, then this tool&quot;) is left alone. Plus <code>TOOL_DEF_INJECTION</code> for a definition claiming priority over the user. Guards now receive the tool, so a rule can ask whether a named identifier is the tool's own. Written from half of MCPTox's servers (Wang et al., AAAI 2026) and reported on the other half: v10 blocks 171 of the 218 held-out poisoned tools (0.8.2: 26), none of the 45 clean MCPTox servers, and the same 3 corpus servers as v8. Tests: <code>test/ruleset-v10.test.ts</code> (attacks from the dev half, honest corpus sentences early drafts blocked).</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Opt-in classifier</strong> (<code>--classifier-url</code>, <code>--classifier-model</code>, <code>--classifier-blocks</code>; key from <code>WARDEN_CLASSIFIER_API_KEY</code>; also in the Action and, through <code>WARDEN_CLASSIFIER_*</code>, the agent-host hooks). Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint, local or hosted. Same prompt, categories and answer format as the HISTOR log's classifier; the tool text is fenced by a per-request random marker and the model's answer is validated as untrusted. Advisory unless <code>--classifier-blocks</code>; a classifier that does not answer is reported and never blocks. <code>--histor</code> also surfaces the log's stored classifier verdict on the tool set you were served (<code>HISTOR_CLASSIFIER</code>, advisory).</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Ruleset v9</strong> (intermediate, never published; 32 rules, 21 block / 11 advise, 23 cover the name). Six blocking rules from a comparison with two other scanners on attack sets: a phrase or a mailbox in &quot;send … to <!-- raw HTML omitted -->&quot; (the object must name the user's data; RFC 2606 placeholder hosts and refusals are left alone); <code>bcc &lt;mailbox&gt;</code>; the conversation itself sent out, only when the same clause moves it and an outside address, a credential or a concealment cue goes with it; concealment whose target is the tool's own behaviour (&quot;do not tell the user about this / that this tool&quot;, &quot;do not mention that you&quot;); a recursive delete of <code>~</code> or <code>/</code>. The harvest rule's window now crosses the dots of a path (<code>read ~/.aws/credentials</code>) and names <code>~/.kube/config</code>, <code>application_default_credentials</code>, <code>.docker/config.json</code>, <code>.git-credentials</code>, <code>.netrc</code>, <code>.pgpass</code>, <code>.npmrc</code>, <code>.pypirc</code>. A tool name is also read as the words it spells (<code>ignore_previous_instructions</code>). On the committed corpus v9 blocks the same 3 servers as v8 and 1 of the 41 carry-over servers; an early draft blocked four more, and those sentences are regression tests in <code>test/ruleset-v9.test.ts</code>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><code>warden-mcp scan</code></strong> reads the MCP configs of Claude Code (<code>.mcp.json</code>, <code>~/.claude.json</code>), Claude Desktop, Cursor, VS Code (JSONC) and Windsurf, connects to every server they start (stdio, streamable HTTP, legacy HTTP+SSE), lists every page of tools, and runs the gate chain on them and on <code>initialize.instructions</code>. It never calls a tool. A table, <code>--json</code>, <code>--json-file</code>, <code>--sarif</code> (2.1.0, blocking findings only, located at the server's line) and <code>--markdown</code>. Exit 0 / 1 (blocked; or <code>--fail-on-error</code> and unchecked) / 2 (usage). Disabled entries, <code>${input:…}</code> entries and entries without command or url are listed as skipped. A server started through <code>wrap</code> is scanned behind the wrapper under <code>wrap</code>'s own pin id; <code>scan</code> reads those pins and never writes any.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><code>--no-launch</code></strong> vets stdio launch lines without starting anything; <strong><code>--public-only</code></strong> refuses remote servers that resolve to loopback, private, link-local, CGNAT or metadata addresses, checked on the address actually dialled; redirects are not followed; responses are bounded.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Lock file</strong> (<code>--lock warden.lock.json</code>, <code>--update-lock</code>): reviewed launch identity and full tool definitions per server, sorted and stable so re-running changes nothing. Blocks <code>LOCK_MISSING</code>, <code>SERVER_IDENTITY_DRIFT</code> and <code>TOOL_DEF_DRIFT</code>, and the Markdown report shows the change as a diff. <code>--update-lock</code> refuses to record a server WARDEN blocks and keeps the reviewed entry.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><code>--histor</code></strong> asks the HISTOR transparency log whether each remote server served this machine the tool set it serves everyone. Sends the endpoint (scheme, host, path; no query, no credentials) and the MTL/1 digest only; never tool text, headers or stdio servers; skips private hosts and key-shaped paths. Advisory <code>HISTOR_UNSEEN_TOOLSET</code> / <code>HISTOR_OLDER_TOOLSET</code>; never blocks. The MTL/1 digest is checked against HISTOR's own implementation (<code>test/fixtures/mtl-vectors.json</code>).</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Credentials in launch lines and URLs are shown as <code>***</code>; untrusted names and descriptions are escaped in the table and cannot leave their code spans and blocks in Markdown.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>GitHub Action</strong> (<code>action.yml</code>, <code>uses: alexar76/warden@v0.9.0</code>): project configs, stdio not started by default, <code>--public-only</code> by default, lock when present, job summary, outputs <code>blocked</code> / <code>servers</code> / <code>sarif</code>, optional SARIF upload. Inputs reach the script as environment variables only.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>pre-commit</strong> (<code>.pre-commit-hooks.yaml</code>): <code>warden-scan</code> (changed configs, no launch) and <code>warden-lock</code> (the project matches <code>warden.lock.json</code>). They run the published package through <code>npx</code>; npm cannot build a TypeScript git dependency installed globally.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Claude Code plugin</strong> (<code>claude-plugin/</code>, marketplace in <code>.claude-plugin/marketplace.json</code>): <code>SessionStart</code> scans the project's servers and tells the user and the model which are blocked, by name and code only; <code>PreToolUse</code> on <code>mcp__.*</code> denies calls to blocked servers and tools from a small verdict file, with a dependency-free script whose decisions are tested against the package's. <code>/warden:scan</code> skill. <code>warden-mcp hook session-start|pre-tool-use</code> are the same hooks as CLI commands.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>wrap</code> and <code>scan</code> share one <code>tools/list</code> collector (<code>src/tool-list.ts</code>). <code>prepare</code> builds <code>dist/</code>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li>See full diff in <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/warden/commits/v0.9.0\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Install script changes</summary>\n<p>This version adds <code>prepare</code> script that runs during installation. Review the package contents before updating.</p>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `@noble/post-quantum` from 0.6.1 to 0.7.1\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/releases\">@​noble/post-quantum's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.7.1</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Added <code>@noble/post-quantum/webcrypto.js</code>, an async noble-style wrapper around the experimental built-in WebCrypto implementations of ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, ML-KEM-1024, and ML-KEM-768 + X25519. It supports deterministic raw-seed key generation, public-key derivation, encapsulation, decapsulation, and a memoized <code>isSupported()</code> probe that performs a complete round trip instead of checking method presence alone.</li>\n<li>Snapshot all options to ensure they're not mutated later</li>\n<li>Snapshot msg in <code>falcon*.attached.open()</code></li>\n<li>Ensure <code>falcon*.attached.open()</code> throws correct error for malformed sig / pubkey</li>\n<li><code>combineKEMS()</code> and <code>combineSigners()</code> now expect valid byte arrays</li>\n<li>Enforce digest lengths promised by pre-hash XOF OIDs: 32b for SHAKE128, 64b for SHAKE256</li>\n<li>Improve zeroization</li>\n<li>Improve Falcon signing and parsing: imported compact secret keys are rejected when the reconstructed sampler deviation is outside Falcon's proof interval</li>\n<li>Harden WebCrypto input validation</li>\n<li>Upgraded noble dependencies to 2.4.0</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Special thanks to Leon Acosta (from QuantaKrypto audits).</p>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/compare/0.7.0...0.7.1\">https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/compare/0.7.0...0.7.1</a></p>\n<h2>0.7.0</h2>\n<h3>Breaking</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><code>hybrid</code>: legacy aliases removed.</strong> <code>XWing</code>/<code>MLKEM768X25519</code> → <code>ml_kem768_x25519</code>, <code>MLKEM768P256</code> → <code>ml_kem768_p256</code>, <code>MLKEM1024P384</code> → <code>ml_kem1024_p384</code>, <code>QSFMLKEM768P256</code> → <code>QSF_ml_kem768_p256</code>, <code>QSFMLKEM1024P384</code> → <code>QSF_ml_kem1024_p384</code>, <code>KitchenSinkMLKEM768X25519</code> → <code>KitchenSink_ml_kem768_x25519</code>.</li>\n<li><strong><code>utils</code>: <code>afunction</code> no longer exported</strong> — moved to <code>@noble/curves/utils.js</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Other</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Falcon: Fix length check in detached (non-default) falcon</li>\n<li><strong><code>MultiplyNTTs</code> intermediate overflow</strong> — <code>a1*b1*zeta</code> could reach ~2³⁵; now <code>mod(mod(a1*b1)*zeta + a0*b0)</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>ML-DSA <code>sign</code> entropy ordering</strong> — randomness drawn before secret-key decoding, so an RNG throw can't leave partially-decoded key material live.</li>\n<li>ML-DSA <code>externalMu</code> length-checks <code>msg</code> as 64-byte µ; ML-KEM detaches the caller's public key before caching; <code>equalBytes</code> validates its inputs; stricter checks and messages throughout.</li>\n<li>Up to 2x speed boost for SLH-DSA</li>\n<li>+16-42% speed boost for hybrid ml-kem-768+x25519</li>\n<li>Upgrade noble deps to 2.3.0</li>\n<li>Reduce on-disk unpacked size, 813kb → 654kb (-159kb): by disabling source maps (they became less relevant).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/compare/2.2.0...2.3.0\">https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/compare/2.2.0...2.3.0</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">@​noble/post-quantum's changelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.7.1 (2026-08-27)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Added <code>@noble/post-quantum/gwebcrypto.js</code>, an async noble-style wrapper around the experimental built-in WebCrypto implementations of ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, ML-KEM-1024, and ML-KEM-768 + X25519. It supports deterministic raw-seed key generation, public-key derivation, encapsulation, decapsulation, and a memoized <code>isSupported()</code> probe that performs a complete round trip instead of checking method presence alone.</li>\n<li>Snapshot all options to ensure they're not mutated later</li>\n<li>Snapshot msg in <code>falcon*.attached.open()</code></li>\n<li>Ensure <code>falcon*.attached.open()</code> throws correct error for malformed sig / pubkey</li>\n<li><code>combineKEMS()</code> and <code>combineSigners()</code> now expect valid byte arrays</li>\n<li>Enforce digest lengths promised by pre-hash XOF OIDs: 32b for SHAKE128, 64b for SHAKE256</li>\n<li>Improve zeroization</li>\n<li>Improve Falcon signing and parsing: imported compact secret keys are rejected when the reconstructed sampler deviation is outside Falcon's proof interval</li>\n<li>Harden WebCrypto input validation</li>\n<li>Upgraded noble dependencies to 2.4.0</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Special thanks to Leon Acosta (from QuantaKrypto audits).</p>\n<h2>0.7.0 (2026-08-09)</h2>\n<h3>Breaking changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Removed legacy <code>hybrid</code> aliases:\n<ul>\n<li><code>XWing</code> and <code>MLKEM768X25519</code> → <code>ml_kem768_x25519</code>.</li>\n<li><code>MLKEM768P256</code> → <code>ml_kem768_p256</code>.</li>\n<li><code>MLKEM1024P384</code> → <code>ml_kem1024_p384</code>.</li>\n<li><code>QSFMLKEM768P256</code> → <code>QSF_ml_kem768_p256</code>.</li>\n<li><code>QSFMLKEM1024P384</code> → <code>QSF_ml_kem1024_p384</code>.</li>\n<li><code>KitchenSinkMLKEM768X25519</code> → <code>KitchenSink_ml_kem768_x25519</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Stopped exporting <code>afunction</code> from <code>utils</code>; it moved to <code>@noble/curves/utils.js</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Other changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fixed the length check in detached, non-default Falcon.</li>\n<li>Fixed an intermediate overflow in <code>MultiplyNTTs</code>, where <code>a1 * b1 * zeta</code> could reach approximately 2³⁵.</li>\n<li>Changed ML-DSA signing to draw entropy before decoding the secret key, so an RNG exception cannot leave partially decoded key material live.</li>\n<li>Made ML-DSA <code>externalMu</code> require a 64-byte <code>msg</code> value.</li>\n<li>Made ML-KEM detach the caller's public key before caching it.</li>\n<li>Made <code>equalBytes</code> validate its inputs and tightened other checks and error messages.</li>\n<li>Improved SLH-DSA performance by up to 2×.</li>\n<li>Improved hybrid ML-KEM-768 and X25519 performance by 16–42%.</li>\n<li>Upgraded noble dependencies to 2.3.0.</li>\n<li>Reduced unpacked package size from 813 KB to 654 KB by disabling source maps.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/commit/a23736036d4d5b34dd3a9e0ee312fd43d00154ac\"><code>a237360</code></a> Release 0.7.1.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/commit/89ddfa0c444ae24c2f184dcaaae97f5e35fea2c8\"><code>89ddfa0</code></a> Bump all deps</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/commit/20039f77e76f8e97ba281e0b9c0ec311f57e96cd\"><code>20039f7</code></a> Add changelog</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/commit/3b5f1982262ee210598d2a8a5f49ed6f7c7f0e2a\"><code>3b5f198</code></a> Bump ci workflows</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/commit/fbd31fdae922f4ec0db69c220fd80cdbc081f4e1\"><code>fbd31fd</code></a> Rename workflow</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/commit/07a8a15058e06cd7f125ca969d32d1be9d8f7842\"><code>07a8a15</code></a> Add fuzzing</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/commit/cf4cc8f7babca87566711c0624ac20f398e2be79\"><code>cf4cc8f</code></a> Fix tests</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/commit/4553bad3cb96164654b536754923291bf48acac8\"><code>4553bad</code></a> webcrypto: validate KEM outputs</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/commit/75626a26e81d75da441a3d6b15c9414230370a15\"><code>75626a2</code></a> hybrid: harden composition</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/commit/1942fa11c00c1a56cbe21bee3bfbd4e4ae9ef289\"><code>1942fa1</code></a> falcon: harden signature handling</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/compare/0.6.1...0.7.1\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `@aimarket/agent` from 0.1.0 to 0.2.1\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/releases\">@​aimarket/agent's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v0.2.1</h2>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/commits/v0.2.1\">https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/commits/v0.2.1</a></p>\n<h2>v0.1.1</h2>\n<h1>aimarket-sdks v0.1.1</h1>\n<p>Release from the AICOM monorepo mirror (<code>main</code>), capturing changes since 2026-05-29.</p>\n<h2>Changes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>feat(aimarket): Pay-on-Verified settlement — Metis-gated escrow on paid invokes</li>\n<li>feat(ecosystem): THEOROS collab on landing, relay scout ops, fleet updates</li>\n<li>fix(security): full ecosystem audit — 43 verified findings across two passes</li>\n<li>fix(docs): point satellite markdown links at GitHub repos</li>\n<li>feat(oracles): 17-oracle family (6 new) + ARGUS conscience, live 3D previews</li>\n<li>fix(ops): VPS deploy hardening, Hub invoke gateway, and SDK/docs audit follow-ups</li>\n<li>feat(monitor): add ARGUS node; docs: 11 oracles everywhere</li>\n<li>docs+ops: trilingual SDK/ecosystem guides + LIVE-against-Base deploy + realistic UNI cadence</li>\n<li>fix(B): real vscode patch apply + SDK TEE pre-invoke verify + honest TEE test</li>\n<li>fix(sdks): unwrap hub channel envelope in TS/Dart/Rust (cohesion)</li>\n<li>cohesion: fix clear-cut ecosystem integrity findings</li>\n<li>security/quality: fix audit findings across the ecosystem</li>\n<li>feat(aimarket-sdks): ecosystem parity guard + registry publish readiness</li>\n<li>feat: standardize badges, CI coverage scripts, and docs across all satellites</li>\n<li>fix(aimarket-sdks): pad Ethereum wallet private key to 32 bytes in Dart</li>\n<li>feat(aimarket-sdks): production Ed25519 and EIP-712 crypto across Dart, TS, and Rust.</li>\n<li>fix: security audit — remove remaining 'plain words' references from bootstrap scripts and value.md headings</li>\n<li>Link all product READMEs to the public ecosystem landing page.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Source: monorepo path <code>aimarket-sdks</code> · <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks\">https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/commit/b3b8cd60f13ae919015fb06756119707135bf313\"><code>b3b8cd6</code></a> chore(satellite): sync aimarket-sdks from aicom monorepo</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/compare/v0.1.0...v0.2.1\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `tsx` from 4.22.4 to 4.23.15\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/releases\">tsx's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v4.23.15</h2>\n<h2><a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/compare/v4.23.14...v4.23.15\">4.23.15</a> (2026-09-20)</h2>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>exclude bare builtins from namespace inheritance (<a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/38e158857e50bca311be7c232a5057e5a2e5347a\">38e1588</a>)</li>\n<li>expose require.cache and require.extensions to tsImport CommonJS modules (<a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/2da34075afaed43e2b7fd0aca5fbebaaf337ff3a\">2da3407</a>)</li>\n<li>make namespaced register() overloads portable for declaration emit (<a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/562c434a5c8695e74327bbeb51cfeb9b86fc7e15\">562c434</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p>This release is also available on:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/tsx/v/4.23.15\"><code>npm package (@​latest dist-tag)</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v4.23.14</h2>\n<h2><a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/compare/v4.23.13...v4.23.14\">4.23.14</a> (2026-09-20)</h2>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>restore the CJS bridge namespace for Node 24 require(esm) under tsImport() (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/privatenumber/tsx/issues/802\">#802</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/6e5236b065738d3687a06396d064774cfede390f\">6e5236b</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p>This release is also available on:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/tsx/v/4.23.14\"><code>npm package (@​latest dist-tag)</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v4.23.13</h2>\n<h2><a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/compare/v4.23.12...v4.23.13\">4.23.13</a> (2026-08-30)</h2>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>cache:</strong> bound shared transform cache memory (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/privatenumber/tsx/issues/835\">#835</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/28e1f12d04cd2afe1db17f8555b14fe5fb567c6e\">28e1f12</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p>This release is also available on:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/tsx/v/4.23.13\"><code>npm package (@​latest dist-tag)</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v4.23.12</h2>\n<h2><a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/compare/v4.23.11...v4.23.12\">4.23.12</a> (2026-08-10)</h2>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>shim <code>import.meta</code> when tokens are split by comments or newlines (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/privatenumber/tsx/issues/829\">#829</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/ed9d33046a135de13a35fdfce12368b79d1b1518\">ed9d330</a>), closes <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/privatenumber/tsx/issues/828\">#828</a></li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p>This release is also available on:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/tsx/v/4.23.12\"><code>npm package (@​latest dist-tag)</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/ca66105a17a2a4c6503fe3a12b5b9ec408286011\"><code>ca66105</code></a> test: fix drive-less file URLs in ESM resolver fixtures</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/2da34075afaed43e2b7fd0aca5fbebaaf337ff3a\"><code>2da3407</code></a> fix: expose require.cache and require.extensions to tsImport CommonJS modules</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/38e158857e50bca311be7c232a5057e5a2e5347a\"><code>38e1588</code></a> fix: exclude bare builtins from namespace inheritance</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/562c434a5c8695e74327bbeb51cfeb9b86fc7e15\"><code>562c434</code></a> fix: make namespaced register() overloads portable for declaration emit</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/edfb1f05a3f40b879a41a03a0801c2abd3a3ecf9\"><code>edfb1f0</code></a> build: upgrade pkgroll and externalize CJS loader reference</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/70e78284837c859f09b96cd10cd71d007aa4b795\"><code>70e7828</code></a> test: upgrade tinyspy for disposable API</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/9ed2022dfa9ea1be9511fe6abcde8110c25055a7\"><code>9ed2022</code></a> ci: avoid duplicate release notifications</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/872e77ffc5e96ca5c4727e74c0694debcb26219b\"><code>872e77f</code></a> refactor: use disposables for cleanup</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/6e5236b065738d3687a06396d064774cfede390f\"><code>6e5236b</code></a> fix: restore the CJS bridge namespace for Node 24 require(esm) under tsImport...</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/28e1f12d04cd2afe1db17f8555b14fe5fb567c6e\"><code>28e1f12</code></a> fix(cache): bound shared transform cache memory (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/privatenumber/tsx/issues/835\">#835</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/compare/v4.22.4...v4.23.15\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't alter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting `@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits that have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all of the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> major version` will close this group update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific dependency's major version (unless you unignore this specific dependency's major version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> minor version` will close this group update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific dependency's minor version (unless you unignore this specific dependency's minor version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name>` will close this group update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific dependency (unless you unignore this specific dependency or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name>` will remove all of the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name> <ignore condition>` will remove the ignore condition of the specified dependency and ignore conditions\n\n\n</details>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/argus/issues/8/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/argus/issues/8/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aimarket-hub/issues/10","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aimarket-hub","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aimarket-hub/issues/10/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aimarket-hub/issues/10/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aimarket-hub/issues/10/events","html_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/pull/10","id":5768326237,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSlJwMM8AAAABHaTO9A","number":10,"title":"chore(deps): bump react and @types/react in /hephaestus/studio","user":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11914280929,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSlJwMM8AAAACxiV_4Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aimarket-hub/labels/dependencies","name":"dependencies","color":"0366d6","default":false,"description":"Pull requests that update a dependency file","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":11914280932,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSlJwMM8AAAACxiV_5A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aimarket-hub/labels/javascript","name":"javascript","color":"168700","default":false,"description":"Pull requests that update javascript code","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-10-08T20:18:12Z","updated_at":"2026-10-10T15:54:59Z","closed_at":"2026-10-10T15:54:48Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aimarket-hub/pulls/10","html_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/pull/10","diff_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/pull/10.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/pull/10.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Bumps [react](https://github.com/react/react/tree/HEAD/packages/react) and [@types/react](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/tree/HEAD/types/react). These dependencies needed to be updated together.\nUpdates `react` from 18.3.1 to 19.3.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/react/react/releases\">react's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>19.3.0 (September 9, 2026)</h2>\n<p>Below is a list of all new features, APIs, and bug fixes.</p>\n<p>Read the <a href=\"https://react.dev/blog/2026/09/09/react-19-3\">React 19.3 release post</a> for more information.</p>\n<h2>New React Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>&lt;ViewTransition /&gt;</code>: Adds <code>&lt;ViewTransition /&gt;</code> and <code>addTransitionType</code> APIs to power View Transition animations in React (<a href=\"https://github.com/sebmarkbage\"><code>@​sebmarkbage</code></a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/jackpope\"><code>@​jackpope</code></a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/gaearon\"><code>@​gaearon</code></a>: <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/31975\">#31975</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/31987\">#31987</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/31996\">#31996</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/31999\">#31999</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32001\">#32001</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32002\">#32002</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32028\">#32028</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32029\">#32029</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32031\">#32031</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32034\">#32034</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32038\">#32038</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32041\">#32041</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32050\">#32050</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32090\">#32090</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32105\">#32105</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32254\">#32254</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32379\">#32379</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32422\">#32422</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32462\">#32462</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32540\">#32540</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32545\">#32545</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32585\">#32585</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32599\">#32599</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32611\">#32611</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32612\">#32612</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32617\">#32617</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32651\">#32651</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32653\">#32653</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32656\">#32656</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32664\">#32664</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32699\">#32699</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32723\">#32723</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32734\">#32734</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32751\">#32751</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32752\">#32752</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32760\">#32760</a>, <a href=\"https:/