-10-10T15:54:58Z","closed_at":"2026-10-10T15:54:48Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aimarket-hub/pulls/11","html_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/pull/11","diff_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/pull/11.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/pull/11.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Bumps [react-dom](https://github.com/react/react/tree/HEAD/packages/react-dom) and [@types/react-dom](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/tree/HEAD/types/react-dom). These dependencies needed to be updated together.\nUpdates `react-dom` from 18.3.1 to 19.3.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/react/react/releases\">react-dom's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>19.3.0 (September 9, 2026)</h2>\n<p>Below is a list of all new features, APIs, and bug fixes.</p>\n<p>Read the <a href=\"https://react.dev/blog/2026/09/09/react-19-3\">React 19.3 release post</a> for more information.</p>\n<h2>New React Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>&lt;ViewTransition /&gt;</code>: Adds <code>&lt;ViewTransition /&gt;</code> and <code>addTransitionType</code> APIs to power View Transition animations in React (<a href=\"https://github.com/sebmarkbage\"><code>@​sebmarkbage</code></a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/jackpope\"><code>@​jackpope</code></a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/gaearon\"><code>@​gaearon</code></a>: <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/31975\">#31975</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/31987\">#31987</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/31996\">#31996</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/31999\">#31999</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32001\">#32001</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32002\">#32002</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32028\">#32028</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32029\">#32029</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32031\">#32031</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32034\">#32034</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32038\">#32038</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32041\">#32041</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32050\">#32050</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32090\">#32090</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32105\">#32105</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32254\">#32254</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32379\">#32379</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32422\">#32422</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32462\">#32462</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32540\">#32540</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32545\">#32545</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32585\">#32585</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32599\">#32599</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32611\">#32611</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32612\">#32612</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32617\">#32617</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32651\">#32651</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32653\">#32653</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32656\">#32656</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32664\">#32664</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32699\">#32699</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32723\">#32723</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32734\">#32734</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32751\">#32751</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32752\">#32752</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32760\">#32760</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32761\">#32761</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32764\">#32764</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32772\">#32772</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32790\">#32790</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32819\">#32819</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32820\">#32820</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32822\">#32822</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32833\">#32833</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32849\">#32849</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/33094\">#33094</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/33191\">#33191</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/33200\">#33200</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/33206\">#33206</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/33293\">#33293</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/33330\">#33330</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/33331\">#33331</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/33332\">#33332</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/33357\">#33357</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/33362\">#33362</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/33433\">#33433</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/33576\">#33576</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34374\">#34374</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34450\">#34450</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34481\">#34481</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34500\">#34500</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34502\">#34502</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34510\">#34510</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34511\">#34511</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34539\">#34539</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35567\">#35567</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35564\">#35564</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35485\">#35485</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35380\">#35380</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35063\">#35063</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35060\">#35060</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34676\">#34676</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/36917\">#36917</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35337\">#35337</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35520\">#35520</a>)</li>\n<li>Fragment Refs: Add Refs to <code>&lt;Fragment /&gt;</code> to support composable platform behavior (<a href=\"https://github.com/jackpope\"><code>@​jackpope</code></a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/sebmarkbage\"><code>@​sebmarkbage</code></a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/eps1lon\"><code>@​eps1lon</code></a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/Dhakshin2007\"><code>@​Dhakshin2007</code></a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/chirokas\"><code>@​chirokas</code></a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/teamleaderleo\"><code>@​teamleaderleo</code></a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/fallintoplace\"><code>@​fallintoplace</code></a>: <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32465\">#32465</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32613\">#32613</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32619\">#32619</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32654\">#32654</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32660\">#32660</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32682\">#32682</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32722\">#32722</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32813\">#32813</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32814\">#32814</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/33056\">#33056</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/33058\">#33058</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/33093\">#33093</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34069\">#34069</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34103\">#34103</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34544\">#34544</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34545\">#34545</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37062\">#37062</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37061\">#37061</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37060\">#37060</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/36047\">#36047</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/36010\">#36010</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35642\">#35642</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35641\">#35641</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35637\">#35637</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35630\">#35630</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34935\">#34935</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37457\">#37457</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37408\">#37408</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37326\">#37326</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37251\">#37251</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37171\">#37171</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37169\">#37169</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37168\">#37168</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37167\">#37167</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37166\">#37166</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37165\">#37165</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37164\">#37164</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37163\">#37163</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37162\">#37162</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37161\">#37161</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37160\">#37160</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37125\">#37125</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37063\">#37063</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>New React DOM Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>browser()</code>: a new <code>react-dom</code> API that returns a usable which errors during server rendering and resolves in the browser. <code>use(browser())</code> inside a <code>&lt;Suspense&gt;</code> boundary marks a subtree as browser-only without reporting a recoverable error (<a href=\"https://github.com/gnoff\"><code>@​gnoff</code></a>: <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37143\">#37143</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37241\">#37241</a>)\n<ul>\n<li>Added an <code>onBrowserBailout</code> option to the <code>react-dom/server</code> APIs to observe when a subtree defers to the browser (<a href=\"https://github.com/gnoff\"><code>@​gnoff</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37193\">#37193</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Notable changes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Enable Trusted Types API integration (<a href=\"https://github.com/rickhanlonii\"><code>@​rickhanlonii</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35816\">#35816</a>)</li>\n<li>Transitions now render independently instead of being entangled into a single render, so a slow transition no longer holds up unrelated ones (<a href=\"https://github.com/acdlite\"><code>@​acdlite</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37290\">#37290</a>)</li>\n<li>Added a DEV-only warning when a component appears to have been unblocked by calling <code>use()</code> conditionally (<a href=\"https://github.com/hoxyq\"><code>@​hoxyq</code></a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/eps1lon\"><code>@​eps1lon</code></a>: <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37104\">#37104</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37203\">#37203</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37491\">#37491</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>All Changes</h2>\n<h3>React</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fast Refresh Fixes\n<ul>\n<li>Fix Fast Refresh to find and remount edits to components wrapped behind <code>lazy()</code> (<a href=\"https://github.com/sophiebits\"><code>@​sophiebits</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/36965\">#36965</a>)</li>\n<li>Fix Fast Refresh so edits to a <code>memo()</code> comparison function take effect (<a href=\"https://github.com/sophiebits\"><code>@​sophiebits</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/36964\">#36964</a>)</li>\n<li>Fix Fast Refresh crash when an edit changes the kind of a component's type (<a href=\"https://github.com/sophiebits\"><code>@​sophiebits</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/36963\">#36963</a>)</li>\n<li>Unify hot reload type resolution for Fast Refresh (<a href=\"https://github.com/sophiebits\"><code>@​sophiebits</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/36962\">#36962</a>)</li>\n<li>Fix Fast Refresh to remount correctly when an edit changes the component kind (<a href=\"https://github.com/sophiebits\"><code>@​sophiebits</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/36950\">#36950</a>)</li>\n<li>Double invoke effects in StrictMode after Fast Refresh (<a href=\"https://github.com/eps1lon\"><code>@​eps1lon</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35962\">#35962</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Performance Track Fixes\n<ul>\n<li>Prevent crash when accessing <code>$$typeof</code> in Performance Tracks (<a href=\"https://github.com/eps1lon\"><code>@​eps1lon</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35679\">#35679</a>)</li>\n<li>Handle non-string function names in Performance Tracks (<a href=\"https://github.com/eps1lon\"><code>@​eps1lon</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35659\">#35659</a>)</li>\n<li>Use minus (<code>-</code>) instead of en dash for removed props in Performance Tracks (<a href=\"https://github.com/eps1lon\"><code>@​eps1lon</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35649\">#35649</a>)</li>\n<li>Handle arrays with bigints in deep objects in Performance Tracks (<a href=\"https://github.com/eps1lon\"><code>@​eps1lon</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35648\">#35648</a>)</li>\n<li>Don't enumerate typed array props in Performance Tracks in DEV (<a href=\"https://github.com/UditDewan\"><code>@​UditDewan</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/36913\">#36913</a>)</li>\n<li>Bail out of diffing wide objects and arrays in Performance Tracks (<a href=\"https://github.com/eps1lon\"><code>@​eps1lon</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34742\">#34742</a>)</li>\n<li>Clear potentially large performance measures in DEV (<a href=\"https://github.com/hoxyq\"><code>@​hoxyq</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34803\">#34803</a>)</li>\n<li>Fix missing else branch for renders with no props change in Performance Tracks (<a href=\"https://github.com/hoxyq\"><code>@​hoxyq</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34837\">#34837</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Activity Fixes\n<ul>\n<li>Fix <code>useSyncExternalStore</code> missing store mutations that happened while an Activity tree was hidden (<a href=\"https://github.com/sophiebits\"><code>@​sophiebits</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/36947\">#36947</a>)</li>\n<li>Hide portal contents when an Activity is hidden (<a href=\"https://github.com/acdlite\"><code>@​acdlite</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35091\">#35091</a>)</li>\n<li>Prevent metadata hoisting in hidden <code>&lt;Activity&gt;</code> trees (<a href=\"https://github.com/ronnakamoto\"><code>@​ronnakamoto</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34983\">#34983</a>)</li>\n<li>Prevent errors thrown inside a hidden Activity from escaping to the visible UI (<a href=\"https://github.com/acdlite\"><code>@​acdlite</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35074\">#35074</a>)</li>\n<li>Don't unhide a node if a direct parent Offscreen is still hidden (<a href=\"https://github.com/sebmarkbage\"><code>@​sebmarkbage</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34821\">#34821</a>)</li>\n<li>Don't show internal <code>&lt;Offscreen&gt;</code> component in error messages (<a href=\"https://github.com/rickhanlonii\"><code>@​rickhanlonii</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35763\">#35763</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Warn in DEV when a component appears to have been unblocked by a conditional <code>use()</code> (<a href=\"https://github.com/hoxyq\"><code>@​hoxyq</code></a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/eps1lon\"><code>@​eps1lon</code></a>: <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37104\">#37104</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37203\">#37203</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37491\">#37491</a>)</li>\n<li>Render transitions independently instead of entangling them into a single render (<a href=\"https://github.com/acdlite\"><code>@​acdlite</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37290\">#37290</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/react/react/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">react-dom's changelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>19.3.0 (September 9, 2026)</h2>\n<h3>New React Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><code>&lt;ViewTransition /&gt;</code>: Adds <code>&lt;ViewTransition /&gt;</code> and <code>addTransitionType</code> APIs to power View Transition animations in React (<a href=\"https://github.com/sebmarkbage\"><code>@​sebmarkbage</code></a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/jackpope\"><code>@​jackpope</code></a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/gaearon\"><code>@​gaearon</code></a>: <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/31975\">#31975</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/31987\">#31987</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/31996\">#31996</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/31999\">#31999</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32001\">#32001</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32002\">#32002</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32028\">#32028</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32029\">#32029</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32031\">#32031</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32034\">#32034</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32038\">#32038</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32041\">#32041</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32050\">#32050</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32090\">#32090</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32105\">#32105</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32254\">#32254</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32379\">#32379</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32422\">#32422</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32462\">#32462</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32540\">#32540</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32545\">#32545</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32585\">#32585</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32599\">#32599</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32611\">#32611</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32612\">#32612</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32617\">#32617</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32651\">#32651</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32653\">#32653</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32656\">#32656</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32664\">#32664</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32699\">#32699</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32723\">#32723</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32734\">#32734</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32751\">#32751</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32752\">#32752</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32760\">#32760</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32761\">#32761</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32764\">#32764</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32772\">#32772</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32790\">#32790</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32819\">#32819</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32820\">#32820</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32822\">#32822</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32833\">#32833</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32849\">#32849</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/33094\">#33094</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/33191\">#33191</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/33200\">#33200</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/33206\">#33206</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/33293\">#33293</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/33330\">#33330</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/33331\">#33331</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/33332\">#33332</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/33357\">#33357</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/33362\">#33362</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/33433\">#33433</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/33576\">#33576</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34374\">#34374</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34450\">#34450</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34481\">#34481</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34500\">#34500</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34502\">#34502</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34510\">#34510</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34511\">#34511</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34539\">#34539</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35567\">#35567</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35564\">#35564</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35485\">#35485</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35380\">#35380</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35063\">#35063</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35060\">#35060</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34676\">#34676</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/36917\">#36917</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35337\">#35337</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35520\">#35520</a>)</li>\n<li>Fragment Refs: Add Refs to <code>&lt;Fragment /&gt;</code> to support composable platform behavior (<a href=\"https://github.com/jackpope\"><code>@​jackpope</code></a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/sebmarkbage\"><code>@​sebmarkbage</code></a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/eps1lon\"><code>@​eps1lon</code></a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/Dhakshin2007\"><code>@​Dhakshin2007</code></a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/chirokas\"><code>@​chirokas</code></a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/teamleaderleo\"><code>@​teamleaderleo</code></a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/fallintoplace\"><code>@​fallintoplace</code></a>: <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32465\">#32465</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32613\">#32613</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32619\">#32619</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32654\">#32654</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32660\">#32660</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32682\">#32682</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32722\">#32722</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32813\">#32813</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/32814\">#32814</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/33056\">#33056</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/33058\">#33058</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/33093\">#33093</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34069\">#34069</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34103\">#34103</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34544\">#34544</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34545\">#34545</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37062\">#37062</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37061\">#37061</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37060\">#37060</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/36047\">#36047</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/36010\">#36010</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35642\">#35642</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35641\">#35641</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35637\">#35637</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35630\">#35630</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34935\">#34935</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37457\">#37457</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37408\">#37408</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37326\">#37326</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37251\">#37251</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37171\">#37171</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37169\">#37169</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37168\">#37168</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37167\">#37167</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37166\">#37166</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37165\">#37165</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37164\">#37164</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37163\">#37163</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37162\">#37162</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37161\">#37161</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37160\">#37160</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37125\">#37125</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37063\">#37063</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>New React DOM Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><code>browser()</code>: a new <code>react-dom</code> API that returns a usable which errors during server rendering and resolves in the browser. <code>use(browser())</code> inside a <code>&lt;Suspense&gt;</code> boundary marks a subtree as browser-only without reporting a recoverable error (<a href=\"https://github.com/gnoff\"><code>@​gnoff</code></a>: <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37143\">#37143</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37241\">#37241</a>)\n<ul>\n<li>Added an <code>onBrowserBailout</code> option to the <code>react-dom/server</code> APIs to observe when a subtree defers to the browser (<a href=\"https://github.com/gnoff\"><code>@​gnoff</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37193\">#37193</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Notable changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Enable Trusted Types API integration (<a href=\"https://github.com/rickhanlonii\"><code>@​rickhanlonii</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35816\">#35816</a>)</li>\n<li>Transitions now render independently instead of being entangled into a single render, so a slow transition no longer holds up unrelated ones (<a href=\"https://github.com/acdlite\"><code>@​acdlite</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37290\">#37290</a>)</li>\n<li>Added a DEV-only warning when a component appears to have been unblocked by calling <code>use()</code> conditionally (<a href=\"https://github.com/hoxyq\"><code>@​hoxyq</code></a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/eps1lon\"><code>@​eps1lon</code></a>: <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37104\">#37104</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37203\">#37203</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37491\">#37491</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>All Changes</h3>\n<h4>React</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Fast Refresh Fixes\n<ul>\n<li>Fix Fast Refresh to find and remount edits to components wrapped behind <code>lazy()</code> (<a href=\"https://github.com/sophiebits\"><code>@​sophiebits</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/36965\">#36965</a>)</li>\n<li>Fix Fast Refresh so edits to a <code>memo()</code> comparison function take effect (<a href=\"https://github.com/sophiebits\"><code>@​sophiebits</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/36964\">#36964</a>)</li>\n<li>Fix Fast Refresh crash when an edit changes the kind of a component's type (<a href=\"https://github.com/sophiebits\"><code>@​sophiebits</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/36963\">#36963</a>)</li>\n<li>Unify hot reload type resolution for Fast Refresh (<a href=\"https://github.com/sophiebits\"><code>@​sophiebits</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/36962\">#36962</a>)</li>\n<li>Fix Fast Refresh to remount correctly when an edit changes the component kind (<a href=\"https://github.com/sophiebits\"><code>@​sophiebits</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/36950\">#36950</a>)</li>\n<li>Double invoke effects in StrictMode after Fast Refresh (<a href=\"https://github.com/eps1lon\"><code>@​eps1lon</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35962\">#35962</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Performance Track Fixes\n<ul>\n<li>Prevent crash when accessing <code>$$typeof</code> in Performance Tracks (<a href=\"https://github.com/eps1lon\"><code>@​eps1lon</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35679\">#35679</a>)</li>\n<li>Handle non-string function names in Performance Tracks (<a href=\"https://github.com/eps1lon\"><code>@​eps1lon</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35659\">#35659</a>)</li>\n<li>Use minus (<code>-</code>) instead of en dash for removed props in Performance Tracks (<a href=\"https://github.com/eps1lon\"><code>@​eps1lon</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35649\">#35649</a>)</li>\n<li>Handle arrays with bigints in deep objects in Performance Tracks (<a href=\"https://github.com/eps1lon\"><code>@​eps1lon</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35648\">#35648</a>)</li>\n<li>Don't enumerate typed array props in Performance Tracks in DEV (<a href=\"https://github.com/UditDewan\"><code>@​UditDewan</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/36913\">#36913</a>)</li>\n<li>Bail out of diffing wide objects and arrays in Performance Tracks (<a href=\"https://github.com/eps1lon\"><code>@​eps1lon</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34742\">#34742</a>)</li>\n<li>Clear potentially large performance measures in DEV (<a href=\"https://github.com/hoxyq\"><code>@​hoxyq</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34803\">#34803</a>)</li>\n<li>Fix missing else branch for renders with no props change in Performance Tracks (<a href=\"https://github.com/hoxyq\"><code>@​hoxyq</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34837\">#34837</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Activity Fixes\n<ul>\n<li>Fix <code>useSyncExternalStore</code> missing store mutations that happened while an Activity tree was hidden (<a href=\"https://github.com/sophiebits\"><code>@​sophiebits</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/36947\">#36947</a>)</li>\n<li>Hide portal contents when an Activity is hidden (<a href=\"https://github.com/acdlite\"><code>@​acdlite</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35091\">#35091</a>)</li>\n<li>Prevent metadata hoisting in hidden <code>&lt;Activity&gt;</code> trees (<a href=\"https://github.com/ronnakamoto\"><code>@​ronnakamoto</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34983\">#34983</a>)</li>\n<li>Prevent errors thrown inside a hidden Activity from escaping to the visible UI (<a href=\"https://github.com/acdlite\"><code>@​acdlite</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35074\">#35074</a>)</li>\n<li>Don't unhide a node if a direct parent Offscreen is still hidden (<a href=\"https://github.com/sebmarkbage\"><code>@​sebmarkbage</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/34821\">#34821</a>)</li>\n<li>Don't show internal <code>&lt;Offscreen&gt;</code> component in error messages (<a href=\"https://github.com/rickhanlonii\"><code>@​rickhanlonii</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/35763\">#35763</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Warn in DEV when a component appears to have been unblocked by a conditional <code>use()</code> (<a href=\"https://github.com/hoxyq\"><code>@​hoxyq</code></a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/eps1lon\"><code>@​eps1lon</code></a>: <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37104\">#37104</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37203\">#37203</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37491\">#37491</a>)</li>\n<li>Render transitions independently instead of entangling them into a single render (<a href=\"https://github.com/acdlite\"><code>@​acdlite</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37290\">#37290</a>)</li>\n<li>Fix hang when updating a dehydrated boundary inside a hidden tree (<a href=\"https://github.com/gaearon\"><code>@​gaearon</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37135\">#37135</a>)</li>\n<li>Don't reacquire Host Singletons during dev effect validation (<a href=\"https://github.com/gnoff\"><code>@​gnoff</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37113\">#37113</a>)</li>\n<li>Only remove properties from Host Singletons on release (<a href=\"https://github.com/gnoff\"><code>@​gnoff</code></a> <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/facebook/react/pull/37112\">#37112</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/react/react/commit/f4e439e1980f0748091f7d36c2005f0463197ed7\"><code>f4e439e</code></a> [Fizz] Add <code>nonce</code> to rendered <code>import maps</code> (<a href=\"https://github.com/react/react/tree/HEAD/packages/react-dom/issues/37339\">#37339</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/react/react/commit/21c89c9fa087b23897999a74a378851e3c50b25c\"><code>21c89c9</code></a> [DOM] Clean up Fragment listeners on signal abort (<a href=\"https://github.com/react/react/tree/HEAD/packages/react-dom/issues/37457\">#37457</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/react/react/commit/065bc84eb50914fa1bc60983eac0b0b717186d74\"><code>065bc84</code></a> [DOM] Unobserve fragment IntersectionObserver targets after exit (<a href=\"https://github.com/react/react/tree/HEAD/packages/react-dom/issues/37408\">#37408</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/react/react/commit/ff7445e636429ab26ce3d388535a79c845d88c94\"><code>ff7445e</code></a> [DOM] Update HTML parser rules for new select parser (<a href=\"https://github.com/react/react/tree/HEAD/packages/react-dom/issues/34804\">#34804</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/react/react/commit/2dc7da790d6388b95b83198ca9b588b2ad5f5c0b\"><code>2dc7da7</code></a> [test] Bump Jest to 30.4 (<a href=\"https://github.com/react/react/tree/HEAD/packages/react-dom/issues/37382\">#37382</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/react/react/commit/29d9d3184484b03cb0369e0494617207df777b7a\"><code>29d9d31</code></a> [DOM] Copy <code>source</code> onto the synthetic toggle event (<a href=\"https://github.com/react/react/tree/HEAD/packages/react-dom/issues/37389\">#37389</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/react/react/commit/269bd40a953a5339ad47c643f9b9dbce88ab878d\"><code>269bd40</code></a> [test] Remove the custom <code>toThrow</code> override for legacy V8 error messages (<a href=\"https://github.com/react/react/tree/HEAD/packages/react-dom/issues/37\">#37</a>...</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/react/react/commit/a1124489a5e8f81e16ac957699a60038b965f502\"><code>a112448</code></a> [DOM] Treat omitted Fragment Event listener options same as <code>capture: false</code> ...</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/react/react/commit/3d050805e802e6c340d2f0c0962dd5a1616a44a4\"><code>3d05080</code></a> [Fizz] Construct the render lifetime controller only when it is needed (<a href=\"https://github.com/react/react/tree/HEAD/packages/react-dom/issues/37357\">#37357</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/react/react/commit/77ed3f545226ac9a834db7490a616b650c2a87a8\"><code>77ed3f5</code></a> [Flight/Fizz] Stop the caller's signal from retaining a finished render (<a href=\"https://github.com/react/react/tree/HEAD/packages/react-dom/issues/37315\">#37315</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a href=\"https://github.com/react/react/commits/v19.3.0/packages/react-dom\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Maintainer changes</summary>\n<p>This version was pushed to npm by <a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/~GitHub%20Actions\">GitHub Actions</a>, a new releaser for react-dom since your current version.</p>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `@types/react-dom` from 18.3.7 to 19.3.0\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li>See full diff in <a href=\"https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/commits/HEAD/types/react-dom\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't alter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting `@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits that have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all of the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n\n\n</details>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aimarket-hub/issues/11/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aimarket-hub/issues/11/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aimarket-hub/issues/6","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aimarket-hub","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aimarket-hub/issues/6/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aimarket-hub/issues/6/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aimarket-hub/issues/6/events","html_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/pull/6","id":5768320254,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSlJwMM8AAAABHaS7YQ","number":6,"title":"chore(deps-dev): bump vite from 6.4.4 to 8.3.2 in /hephaestus/studio","user":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11914280929,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSlJwMM8AAAACxiV_4Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aimarket-hub/labels/dependencies","name":"dependencies","color":"0366d6","default":false,"description":"Pull requests that update a dependency file","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":11914280932,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSlJwMM8AAAACxiV_5A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aimarket-hub/labels/javascript","name":"javascript","color":"168700","default":false,"description":"Pull requests that update javascript code","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-10-08T20:17:43Z","updated_at":"2026-10-10T15:54:58Z","closed_at":"2026-10-10T15:54:48Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aimarket-hub/pulls/6","html_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/pull/6","diff_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/pull/6.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/pull/6.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Bumps [vite](https://github.com/vitejs/vite/tree/HEAD/packages/vite) from 6.4.4 to 8.3.2.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/releases\">vite's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v8.3.2</h2>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>build:</strong> preload CSS correctly when <code>renderBuiltUrl</code> returns URLs with queries (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23611\">#23611</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/64e0a215c24f0522b27b91f93cfd93e317b94481\">64e0a21</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>bundled-dev:</strong> serve lazy chunk sourcemaps (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23026\">#23026</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/eb7aa9a8816a1e926d5d9b4cbe7e796b61314ce2\">eb7aa9a</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>bundled-dev:</strong> serve the rolldown runtime from the installed rolldown (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23568\">#23568</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/bc598a6a8a6b7d6e157e9f19c16911cff8d2360c\">bc598a6</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>deps:</strong> update all non-major dependencies (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23601\">#23601</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/9944fa6033873f13ae88f59e023ab642c50fee2b\">9944fa6</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>deps:</strong> update rolldown-related dependencies (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23602\">#23602</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/88c17415af221b3a13e778f4f2c0e907c8287baf\">88c1741</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>html:</strong> resolve percent-encoded srcset urls (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23609\">#23609</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/53f1ce7bfe38426861f6da572ef0e3359f6a80cd\">53f1ce7</a>)</li>\n<li>limit size of object and array printing via <code>forwardConsole</code> (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23565\">#23565</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/e64a5877dd3e552843a545749ccc257568917d28\">e64a587</a>)</li>\n<li>merge <code>build.rolldownOptions.output.minify</code> correctly (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23536\">#23536</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/bba3bb8beedd185948956e02667d450672632d79\">bba3bb8</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>optimize-deps:</strong> avoid &quot;unsupported&quot; warnings for browser:false mappings (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23590\">#23590</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/5e4b9ca3dcb24b51f58a765fd2d852614bbf3574\">5e4b9ca</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>optimizer:</strong> preserve excluded optional peer require fallbacks (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23600\">#23600</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/a2bd6fa897c35c8a691671a7d70061c1cdd5c688\">a2bd6fa</a>)</li>\n<li>pass queries to <code>renderBuiltUrl</code> (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23586\">#23586</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/744269e5b2a155074910ddd275aecf2b83938496\">744269e</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>server:</strong> handle file watcher errors without crashing (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23503\">#23503</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/6894f5cbceac589536a0efb476d881a47f5ab1c5\">6894f5c</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>server:</strong> release previous environments after initialization (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23499\">#23499</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/5a3a010eea4c9ebbdcc080819f93068d4e035bd4\">5a3a010</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>ssr:</strong> encode whitespace in module runner sourceURL (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23513\">#23513</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/bbc88129c967a8b8eedebd93acc82bee63b86b2a\">bbc8812</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>worker:</strong> align worker urls in client and server when using terser (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23614\">#23614</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/24bd3316f3b2503d04a49361e365532bdb335e19\">24bd331</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Performance Improvements</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>avoid encoding intermediate source maps (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23461\">#23461</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/89574f6d940a7273a53c5122a4477285801a696a\">89574f6</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>build:</strong> avoid quadratic link scan in the preload helper (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23510\">#23510</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/cf5c0288d526824aead1b24e977400f13c527927\">cf5c028</a>)</li>\n<li>only register time middleware when debug logging is enabled (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23621\">#23621</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/94d0080345e23d63d4cd02df2f7fa2afae775c26\">94d0080</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>fix dead og-image PNG links in vite6/vite7 changelog entries (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23594\">#23594</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/1929b4cc5f38ad53781e3b07b8bdaa32cf18da07\">1929b4c</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Miscellaneous Chores</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>deps:</strong> update vitest monorepo to v5 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23604\">#23604</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/24339f4339d64fd8b5bc37654ac14ccff5aee584\">24339f4</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Code Refactoring</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>use <code>tinyexec</code> instead of <code>cross-spawn</code> (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23583\">#23583</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/db915e5c0edbe1359dcf0cea340c9571dc7f4ad9\">db915e5</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Tests</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>bundled-dev:</strong> accept a rolldown dev runtime with no helper imports (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23606\">#23606</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/634745dcc5648912bc32cb4de72ed8dd2230efa0\">634745d</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v8.3.1</h2>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>deps:</strong> update all non-major dependencies (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23482\">#23482</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/3c752c8932bc0599465ba4a6d8f44aaf1e934c3d\">3c752c8</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>deps:</strong> update all non-major dependencies (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23537\">#23537</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/e8990c4d6101dfaca2654ed8ab4d0574ee920248\">e8990c4</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>deps:</strong> update rolldown-related dependencies (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23483\">#23483</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/9aecbbfa5fb5da4b9981c099cb9746a9fd210806\">9aecbbf</a>)</li>\n<li>handle <code>server.ws: false</code> in mergeConfig (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23511\">#23511</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/f68c0d5a28c96555431413e3e2cbe644337b087f\">f68c0d5</a>)</li>\n<li>merge <code>build.rolldownOptions.output.comments</code> correctly (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23514\">#23514</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/4aba8d8720e82e4c5b694a4b7877755a3f84fc57\">4aba8d8</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>optimizer:</strong> don't skip imports whose binding starts with type (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23540\">#23540</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/39330f489a0ae08923557f0ce10a307d6662a3f5\">39330f4</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/blob/main/packages/vite/CHANGELOG.md\">vite's changelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2><!-- raw HTML omitted --><a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/compare/v8.3.1...v8.3.2\">8.3.2</a> (2026-10-01)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></h2>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>build:</strong> preload CSS correctly when <code>renderBuiltUrl</code> returns URLs with queries (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23611\">#23611</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/64e0a215c24f0522b27b91f93cfd93e317b94481\">64e0a21</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>bundled-dev:</strong> serve lazy chunk sourcemaps (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23026\">#23026</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/eb7aa9a8816a1e926d5d9b4cbe7e796b61314ce2\">eb7aa9a</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>bundled-dev:</strong> serve the rolldown runtime from the installed rolldown (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23568\">#23568</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/bc598a6a8a6b7d6e157e9f19c16911cff8d2360c\">bc598a6</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>deps:</strong> update all non-major dependencies (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23601\">#23601</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/9944fa6033873f13ae88f59e023ab642c50fee2b\">9944fa6</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>deps:</strong> update rolldown-related dependencies (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23602\">#23602</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/88c17415af221b3a13e778f4f2c0e907c8287baf\">88c1741</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>html:</strong> resolve percent-encoded srcset urls (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23609\">#23609</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/53f1ce7bfe38426861f6da572ef0e3359f6a80cd\">53f1ce7</a>)</li>\n<li>limit size of object and array printing via <code>forwardConsole</code> (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23565\">#23565</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/e64a5877dd3e552843a545749ccc257568917d28\">e64a587</a>)</li>\n<li>merge <code>build.rolldownOptions.output.minify</code> correctly (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23536\">#23536</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/bba3bb8beedd185948956e02667d450672632d79\">bba3bb8</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>optimize-deps:</strong> avoid &quot;unsupported&quot; warnings for browser:false mappings (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23590\">#23590</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/5e4b9ca3dcb24b51f58a765fd2d852614bbf3574\">5e4b9ca</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>optimizer:</strong> preserve excluded optional peer require fallbacks (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23600\">#23600</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/a2bd6fa897c35c8a691671a7d70061c1cdd5c688\">a2bd6fa</a>)</li>\n<li>pass queries to <code>renderBuiltUrl</code> (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23586\">#23586</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/744269e5b2a155074910ddd275aecf2b83938496\">744269e</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>server:</strong> handle file watcher errors without crashing (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23503\">#23503</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/6894f5cbceac589536a0efb476d881a47f5ab1c5\">6894f5c</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>server:</strong> release previous environments after initialization (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23499\">#23499</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/5a3a010eea4c9ebbdcc080819f93068d4e035bd4\">5a3a010</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>ssr:</strong> encode whitespace in module runner sourceURL (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23513\">#23513</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/bbc88129c967a8b8eedebd93acc82bee63b86b2a\">bbc8812</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>worker:</strong> align worker urls in client and server when using terser (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23614\">#23614</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/24bd3316f3b2503d04a49361e365532bdb335e19\">24bd331</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Performance Improvements</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>avoid encoding intermediate source maps (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23461\">#23461</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/89574f6d940a7273a53c5122a4477285801a696a\">89574f6</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>build:</strong> avoid quadratic link scan in the preload helper (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23510\">#23510</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/cf5c0288d526824aead1b24e977400f13c527927\">cf5c028</a>)</li>\n<li>only register time middleware when debug logging is enabled (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23621\">#23621</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/94d0080345e23d63d4cd02df2f7fa2afae775c26\">94d0080</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>fix dead og-image PNG links in vite6/vite7 changelog entries (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23594\">#23594</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/1929b4cc5f38ad53781e3b07b8bdaa32cf18da07\">1929b4c</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Miscellaneous Chores</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>deps:</strong> update vitest monorepo to v5 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23604\">#23604</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/24339f4339d64fd8b5bc37654ac14ccff5aee584\">24339f4</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Code Refactoring</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>use <code>tinyexec</code> instead of <code>cross-spawn</code> (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23583\">#23583</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/db915e5c0edbe1359dcf0cea340c9571dc7f4ad9\">db915e5</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Tests</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>bundled-dev:</strong> accept a rolldown dev runtime with no helper imports (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23606\">#23606</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/634745dcc5648912bc32cb4de72ed8dd2230efa0\">634745d</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><!-- raw HTML omitted --><a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/compare/v8.3.0...v8.3.1\">8.3.1</a> (2026-09-24)<!-- raw HTML omitted --></h2>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>deps:</strong> update all non-major dependencies (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23482\">#23482</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/3c752c8932bc0599465ba4a6d8f44aaf1e934c3d\">3c752c8</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>deps:</strong> update all non-major dependencies (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23537\">#23537</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/e8990c4d6101dfaca2654ed8ab4d0574ee920248\">e8990c4</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>deps:</strong> update rolldown-related dependencies (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23483\">#23483</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/9aecbbfa5fb5da4b9981c099cb9746a9fd210806\">9aecbbf</a>)</li>\n<li>handle <code>server.ws: false</code> in mergeConfig (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23511\">#23511</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/f68c0d5a28c96555431413e3e2cbe644337b087f\">f68c0d5</a>)</li>\n<li>merge <code>build.rolldownOptions.output.comments</code> correctly (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23514\">#23514</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/4aba8d8720e82e4c5b694a4b7877755a3f84fc57\">4aba8d8</a>)</li>\n<li><strong>optimizer:</strong> don't skip imports whose binding starts with type (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/23540\">#23540</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/39330f489a0ae08923557f0ce10a307d6662a3f5\">39330f4</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/10033218d239c927cdc375970b5741cce408e81b\"><code>1003321</code></a> release: v8.3.2 (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/tree/HEAD/packages/vite/issues/23623\">#23623</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/24bd3316f3b2503d04a49361e365532bdb335e19\"><code>24bd331</code></a> fix(worker): align worker urls in client and server when using terser (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/tree/HEAD/packages/vite/issues/23614\">#23614</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/94d0080345e23d63d4cd02df2f7fa2afae775c26\"><code>94d0080</code></a> perf: only register time middleware when debug logging is enabled (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/tree/HEAD/packages/vite/issues/23621\">#23621</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/89574f6d940a7273a53c5122a4477285801a696a\"><code>89574f6</code></a> perf: avoid encoding intermediate source maps (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/tree/HEAD/packages/vite/issues/23461\">#23461</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/5a3a010eea4c9ebbdcc080819f93068d4e035bd4\"><code>5a3a010</code></a> fix(server): release previous environments after initialization (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/tree/HEAD/packages/vite/issues/23499\">#23499</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/1929b4cc5f38ad53781e3b07b8bdaa32cf18da07\"><code>1929b4c</code></a> docs: fix dead og-image PNG links in vite6/vite7 changelog entries (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/tree/HEAD/packages/vite/issues/23594\">#23594</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/6894f5cbceac589536a0efb476d881a47f5ab1c5\"><code>6894f5c</code></a> fix(server): handle file watcher errors without crashing (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/tree/HEAD/packages/vite/issues/23503\">#23503</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/cf5c0288d526824aead1b24e977400f13c527927\"><code>cf5c028</code></a> perf(build): avoid quadratic link scan in the preload helper (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/tree/HEAD/packages/vite/issues/23510\">#23510</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/bba3bb8beedd185948956e02667d450672632d79\"><code>bba3bb8</code></a> fix: merge <code>build.rolldownOptions.output.minify</code> correctly (<a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/tree/HEAD/packages/vite/issues/23536\">#23536</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commit/5e4b9ca3dcb24b51f58a765fd2d852614bbf3574\"><code>5e4b9ca</code></a> fix(optimize-deps): avoid &quot;unsupported&quot; warnings for browser:false mappings (...</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a href=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/commits/v8.3.2/packages/vite\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility score](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=vite&package-manager=npm_and_yarn&previous-version=6.4.4&new-version=8.3.2)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't alter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting `@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits that have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all of the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n\n\n</details>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aimarket-hub/issues/6/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/aimarket-hub/issues/6/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/argus/issues/2","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/argus","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/argus/issues/2/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/argus/issues/2/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/argus/issues/2/events","html_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/argus/pull/2","id":5768354596,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTCxG0M8AAAABHaUrNQ","number":2,"title":"chore(deps): bump the npm-minor-patch group across 1 directory with 3 updates","user":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12603398796,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTCxG0M8AAAAC7ziajA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/argus/labels/dependencies","name":"dependencies","color":"0366d6","default":false,"description":"Pull requests that update a dependency file","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12603398844,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTCxG0M8AAAAC7ziavA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/argus/labels/javascript","name":"javascript","color":"168700","default":false,"description":"Pull requests that update javascript code","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-10-08T20:20:33Z","updated_at":"2026-10-09T13:54:00Z","closed_at":"2026-10-09T13:53:50Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/argus/pulls/2","html_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/argus/pull/2","diff_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/argus/pull/2.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/argus/pull/2.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Bumps the npm-minor-patch group with 3 updates in the / directory: [@noble/post-quantum](https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum), [@aimarket/agent](https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks) and [tsx](https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx).\n\nUpdates `@noble/post-quantum` from 0.6.1 to 0.7.1\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/releases\">@​noble/post-quantum's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.7.1</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Added <code>@noble/post-quantum/webcrypto.js</code>, an async noble-style wrapper around the experimental built-in WebCrypto implementations of ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, ML-KEM-1024, and ML-KEM-768 + X25519. It supports deterministic raw-seed key generation, public-key derivation, encapsulation, decapsulation, and a memoized <code>isSupported()</code> probe that performs a complete round trip instead of checking method presence alone.</li>\n<li>Snapshot all options to ensure they're not mutated later</li>\n<li>Snapshot msg in <code>falcon*.attached.open()</code></li>\n<li>Ensure <code>falcon*.attached.open()</code> throws correct error for malformed sig / pubkey</li>\n<li><code>combineKEMS()</code> and <code>combineSigners()</code> now expect valid byte arrays</li>\n<li>Enforce digest lengths promised by pre-hash XOF OIDs: 32b for SHAKE128, 64b for SHAKE256</li>\n<li>Improve zeroization</li>\n<li>Improve Falcon signing and parsing: imported compact secret keys are rejected when the reconstructed sampler deviation is outside Falcon's proof interval</li>\n<li>Harden WebCrypto input validation</li>\n<li>Upgraded noble dependencies to 2.4.0</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Special thanks to Leon Acosta (from QuantaKrypto audits).</p>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/compare/0.7.0...0.7.1\">https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/compare/0.7.0...0.7.1</a></p>\n<h2>0.7.0</h2>\n<h3>Breaking</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><code>hybrid</code>: legacy aliases removed.</strong> <code>XWing</code>/<code>MLKEM768X25519</code> → <code>ml_kem768_x25519</code>, <code>MLKEM768P256</code> → <code>ml_kem768_p256</code>, <code>MLKEM1024P384</code> → <code>ml_kem1024_p384</code>, <code>QSFMLKEM768P256</code> → <code>QSF_ml_kem768_p256</code>, <code>QSFMLKEM1024P384</code> → <code>QSF_ml_kem1024_p384</code>, <code>KitchenSinkMLKEM768X25519</code> → <code>KitchenSink_ml_kem768_x25519</code>.</li>\n<li><strong><code>utils</code>: <code>afunction</code> no longer exported</strong> — moved to <code>@noble/curves/utils.js</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Other</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Falcon: Fix length check in detached (non-default) falcon</li>\n<li><strong><code>MultiplyNTTs</code> intermediate overflow</strong> — <code>a1*b1*zeta</code> could reach ~2³⁵; now <code>mod(mod(a1*b1)*zeta + a0*b0)</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>ML-DSA <code>sign</code> entropy ordering</strong> — randomness drawn before secret-key decoding, so an RNG throw can't leave partially-decoded key material live.</li>\n<li>ML-DSA <code>externalMu</code> length-checks <code>msg</code> as 64-byte µ; ML-KEM detaches the caller's public key before caching; <code>equalBytes</code> validates its inputs; stricter checks and messages throughout.</li>\n<li>Up to 2x speed boost for SLH-DSA</li>\n<li>+16-42% speed boost for hybrid ml-kem-768+x25519</li>\n<li>Upgrade noble deps to 2.3.0</li>\n<li>Reduce on-disk unpacked size, 813kb → 654kb (-159kb): by disabling source maps (they became less relevant).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/compare/2.2.0...2.3.0\">https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/compare/2.2.0...2.3.0</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">@​noble/post-quantum's changelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.7.1 (2026-08-27)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Added <code>@noble/post-quantum/gwebcrypto.js</code>, an async noble-style wrapper around the experimental built-in WebCrypto implementations of ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, ML-KEM-1024, and ML-KEM-768 + X25519. It supports deterministic raw-seed key generation, public-key derivation, encapsulation, decapsulation, and a memoized <code>isSupported()</code> probe that performs a complete round trip instead of checking method presence alone.</li>\n<li>Snapshot all options to ensure they're not mutated later</li>\n<li>Snapshot msg in <code>falcon*.attached.open()</code></li>\n<li>Ensure <code>falcon*.attached.open()</code> throws correct error for malformed sig / pubkey</li>\n<li><code>combineKEMS()</code> and <code>combineSigners()</code> now expect valid byte arrays</li>\n<li>Enforce digest lengths promised by pre-hash XOF OIDs: 32b for SHAKE128, 64b for SHAKE256</li>\n<li>Improve zeroization</li>\n<li>Improve Falcon signing and parsing: imported compact secret keys are rejected when the reconstructed sampler deviation is outside Falcon's proof interval</li>\n<li>Harden WebCrypto input validation</li>\n<li>Upgraded noble dependencies to 2.4.0</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Special thanks to Leon Acosta (from QuantaKrypto audits).</p>\n<h2>0.7.0 (2026-08-09)</h2>\n<h3>Breaking changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Removed legacy <code>hybrid</code> aliases:\n<ul>\n<li><code>XWing</code> and <code>MLKEM768X25519</code> → <code>ml_kem768_x25519</code>.</li>\n<li><code>MLKEM768P256</code> → <code>ml_kem768_p256</code>.</li>\n<li><code>MLKEM1024P384</code> → <code>ml_kem1024_p384</code>.</li>\n<li><code>QSFMLKEM768P256</code> → <code>QSF_ml_kem768_p256</code>.</li>\n<li><code>QSFMLKEM1024P384</code> → <code>QSF_ml_kem1024_p384</code>.</li>\n<li><code>KitchenSinkMLKEM768X25519</code> → <code>KitchenSink_ml_kem768_x25519</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Stopped exporting <code>afunction</code> from <code>utils</code>; it moved to <code>@noble/curves/utils.js</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Other changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fixed the length check in detached, non-default Falcon.</li>\n<li>Fixed an intermediate overflow in <code>MultiplyNTTs</code>, where <code>a1 * b1 * zeta</code> could reach approximately 2³⁵.</li>\n<li>Changed ML-DSA signing to draw entropy before decoding the secret key, so an RNG exception cannot leave partially decoded key material live.</li>\n<li>Made ML-DSA <code>externalMu</code> require a 64-byte <code>msg</code> value.</li>\n<li>Made ML-KEM detach the caller's public key before caching it.</li>\n<li>Made <code>equalBytes</code> validate its inputs and tightened other checks and error messages.</li>\n<li>Improved SLH-DSA performance by up to 2×.</li>\n<li>Improved hybrid ML-KEM-768 and X25519 performance by 16–42%.</li>\n<li>Upgraded noble dependencies to 2.3.0.</li>\n<li>Reduced unpacked package size from 813 KB to 654 KB by disabling source maps.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/commit/a23736036d4d5b34dd3a9e0ee312fd43d00154ac\"><code>a237360</code></a> Release 0.7.1.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/commit/89ddfa0c444ae24c2f184dcaaae97f5e35fea2c8\"><code>89ddfa0</code></a> Bump all deps</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/commit/20039f77e76f8e97ba281e0b9c0ec311f57e96cd\"><code>20039f7</code></a> Add changelog</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/commit/3b5f1982262ee210598d2a8a5f49ed6f7c7f0e2a\"><code>3b5f198</code></a> Bump ci workflows</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/commit/fbd31fdae922f4ec0db69c220fd80cdbc081f4e1\"><code>fbd31fd</code></a> Rename workflow</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/commit/07a8a15058e06cd7f125ca969d32d1be9d8f7842\"><code>07a8a15</code></a> Add fuzzing</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/commit/cf4cc8f7babca87566711c0624ac20f398e2be79\"><code>cf4cc8f</code></a> Fix tests</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/commit/4553bad3cb96164654b536754923291bf48acac8\"><code>4553bad</code></a> webcrypto: validate KEM outputs</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/commit/75626a26e81d75da441a3d6b15c9414230370a15\"><code>75626a2</code></a> hybrid: harden composition</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/commit/1942fa11c00c1a56cbe21bee3bfbd4e4ae9ef289\"><code>1942fa1</code></a> falcon: harden signature handling</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a href=\"https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum/compare/0.6.1...0.7.1\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `@aimarket/agent` from 0.1.0 to 0.2.1\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/releases\">@​aimarket/agent's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v0.2.1</h2>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/commits/v0.2.1\">https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/commits/v0.2.1</a></p>\n<h2>v0.1.1</h2>\n<h1>aimarket-sdks v0.1.1</h1>\n<p>Release from the AICOM monorepo mirror (<code>main</code>), capturing changes since 2026-05-29.</p>\n<h2>Changes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>feat(aimarket): Pay-on-Verified settlement — Metis-gated escrow on paid invokes</li>\n<li>feat(ecosystem): THEOROS collab on landing, relay scout ops, fleet updates</li>\n<li>fix(security): full ecosystem audit — 43 verified findings across two passes</li>\n<li>fix(docs): point satellite markdown links at GitHub repos</li>\n<li>feat(oracles): 17-oracle family (6 new) + ARGUS conscience, live 3D previews</li>\n<li>fix(ops): VPS deploy hardening, Hub invoke gateway, and SDK/docs audit follow-ups</li>\n<li>feat(monitor): add ARGUS node; docs: 11 oracles everywhere</li>\n<li>docs+ops: trilingual SDK/ecosystem guides + LIVE-against-Base deploy + realistic UNI cadence</li>\n<li>fix(B): real vscode patch apply + SDK TEE pre-invoke verify + honest TEE test</li>\n<li>fix(sdks): unwrap hub channel envelope in TS/Dart/Rust (cohesion)</li>\n<li>cohesion: fix clear-cut ecosystem integrity findings</li>\n<li>security/quality: fix audit findings across the ecosystem</li>\n<li>feat(aimarket-sdks): ecosystem parity guard + registry publish readiness</li>\n<li>feat: standardize badges, CI coverage scripts, and docs across all satellites</li>\n<li>fix(aimarket-sdks): pad Ethereum wallet private key to 32 bytes in Dart</li>\n<li>feat(aimarket-sdks): production Ed25519 and EIP-712 crypto across Dart, TS, and Rust.</li>\n<li>fix: security audit — remove remaining 'plain words' references from bootstrap scripts and value.md headings</li>\n<li>Link all product READMEs to the public ecosystem landing page.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Source: monorepo path <code>aimarket-sdks</code> · <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks\">https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/commit/b3b8cd60f13ae919015fb06756119707135bf313\"><code>b3b8cd6</code></a> chore(satellite): sync aimarket-sdks from aicom monorepo</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks/compare/v0.1.0...v0.2.1\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `tsx` from 4.22.4 to 4.23.15\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/releases\">tsx's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v4.23.15</h2>\n<h2><a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/compare/v4.23.14...v4.23.15\">4.23.15</a> (2026-09-20)</h2>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>exclude bare builtins from namespace inheritance (<a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/38e158857e50bca311be7c232a5057e5a2e5347a\">38e1588</a>)</li>\n<li>expose require.cache and require.extensions to tsImport CommonJS modules (<a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/2da34075afaed43e2b7fd0aca5fbebaaf337ff3a\">2da3407</a>)</li>\n<li>make namespaced register() overloads portable for declaration emit (<a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/562c434a5c8695e74327bbeb51cfeb9b86fc7e15\">562c434</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p>This release is also available on:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/tsx/v/4.23.15\"><code>npm package (@​latest dist-tag)</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v4.23.14</h2>\n<h2><a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/compare/v4.23.13...v4.23.14\">4.23.14</a> (2026-09-20)</h2>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>restore the CJS bridge namespace for Node 24 require(esm) under tsImport() (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/privatenumber/tsx/issues/802\">#802</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/6e5236b065738d3687a06396d064774cfede390f\">6e5236b</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p>This release is also available on:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/tsx/v/4.23.14\"><code>npm package (@​latest dist-tag)</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v4.23.13</h2>\n<h2><a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/compare/v4.23.12...v4.23.13\">4.23.13</a> (2026-08-30)</h2>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>cache:</strong> bound shared transform cache memory (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/privatenumber/tsx/issues/835\">#835</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/28e1f12d04cd2afe1db17f8555b14fe5fb567c6e\">28e1f12</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p>This release is also available on:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/tsx/v/4.23.13\"><code>npm package (@​latest dist-tag)</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v4.23.12</h2>\n<h2><a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/compare/v4.23.11...v4.23.12\">4.23.12</a> (2026-08-10)</h2>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>shim <code>import.meta</code> when tokens are split by comments or newlines (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/privatenumber/tsx/issues/829\">#829</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/ed9d33046a135de13a35fdfce12368b79d1b1518\">ed9d330</a>), closes <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/privatenumber/tsx/issues/828\">#828</a></li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p>This release is also available on:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/tsx/v/4.23.12\"><code>npm package (@​latest dist-tag)</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/ca66105a17a2a4c6503fe3a12b5b9ec408286011\"><code>ca66105</code></a> test: fix drive-less file URLs in ESM resolver fixtures</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/2da34075afaed43e2b7fd0aca5fbebaaf337ff3a\"><code>2da3407</code></a> fix: expose require.cache and require.extensions to tsImport CommonJS modules</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/38e158857e50bca311be7c232a5057e5a2e5347a\"><code>38e1588</code></a> fix: exclude bare builtins from namespace inheritance</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/562c434a5c8695e74327bbeb51cfeb9b86fc7e15\"><code>562c434</code></a> fix: make namespaced register() overloads portable for declaration emit</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/edfb1f05a3f40b879a41a03a0801c2abd3a3ecf9\"><code>edfb1f0</code></a> build: upgrade pkgroll and externalize CJS loader reference</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/70e78284837c859f09b96cd10cd71d007aa4b795\"><code>70e7828</code></a> test: upgrade tinyspy for disposable API</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/9ed2022dfa9ea1be9511fe6abcde8110c25055a7\"><code>9ed2022</code></a> ci: avoid duplicate release notifications</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/872e77ffc5e96ca5c4727e74c0694debcb26219b\"><code>872e77f</code></a> refactor: use disposables for cleanup</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/6e5236b065738d3687a06396d064774cfede390f\"><code>6e5236b</code></a> fix: restore the CJS bridge namespace for Node 24 require(esm) under tsImport...</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/commit/28e1f12d04cd2afe1db17f8555b14fe5fb567c6e\"><code>28e1f12</code></a> fix(cache): bound shared transform cache memory (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/privatenumber/tsx/issues/835\">#835</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a href=\"https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx/compare/v4.22.4...v4.23.15\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't alter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting `@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits that have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all of the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> major version` will close this group update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific dependency's major version (unless you unignore this specific dependency's major version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> minor version` will close this group update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific dependency's minor version (unless you unignore this specific dependency's minor version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name>` will close this group update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific dependency (unless you unignore this specific dependency or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name>` will remove all of the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name> <ignore condition>` will remove the ignore condition of the specified dependency and ignore conditions\n\n\n</details>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/argus/issues/2/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/argus/issues/2/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/histor/issues/6","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/histor","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/histor/issues/6/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/histor/issues/6/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/histor/issues/6/events","html_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/histor/pull/6","id":5660184088,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUnkOyM8AAAABGEK2Dw","number":6,"title":"chore(deps): bump @aimarket/warden from 0.5.0 to 0.6.0 in /scanner","user":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12329216864,"node_id":"LA_kwDOUnkOyM8AAAAC3uDrYA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/histor/labels/dependencies","name":"dependencies","color":"0366d6","default":false,"description":"Pull requests that update a dependency file","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12490101010,"node_id":"LA_kwDOUnkOyM8AAAAC6HfREg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/histor/labels/javascript","name":"javascript","color":"168700","default":false,"description":"Pull requests that update javascript code","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-10-01T09:43:33Z","updated_at":"2026-10-01T20:04:41Z","closed_at":"2026-10-01T20:04:40Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/histor/pulls/6","html_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/histor/pull/6","diff_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/histor/pull/6.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/alexar76/histor/pull/6.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Bumps [@aimarket/warden](https://github.com/alexar76/warden) from 0.5.0 to 0.6.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/warden/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">@​aimarket/warden's changelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.6.0 — 2026-09-23</h2>\n<p>Ruleset <strong>v5</strong>: language-independent coverage. A rule table written in one language cannot read\nmeaning in every other, so v5 strengthens what does not depend on the language at all, and says\nplainly where the table stops.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Text is folded before any rule reads it</strong> (<code>src/fold.ts</code>, published as <code>fold</code> beside the rules\nand part of the digest): NFKC for fullwidth letters, ligatures and other compatibility forms;\ninvisible characters inside a word dropped; the Unicode TAG block (invisible ASCII that can spell a\nwhole sentence) decoded; look-alike Cyrillic/Greek letters mapped to Latin inside a word that\nalready mixes scripts, while text written wholly in one script is left alone. An English rule can\nno longer be dodged by <code>ｉｇｎｏｒｅ</code>, a zero-width space inside the word, tag characters or a Cyrillic\n<code>о</code>. The two hidden-payload rules read the raw text (<code>raw: true</code> in the published table).</li>\n<li><strong><code>TOOL_DEF_HIDDEN_UNICODE</code></strong> now also catches the Unicode-tag block and the bidi isolates\n(U+2066–2069). <code>displaySafe</code> escapes tag characters, so a finding never prints them invisibly.</li>\n<li><strong><code>TOOL_DEF_SECRET_EXFIL</code></strong> (new, advisory): a secret store (<code>.env</code>, <code>~/.ssh/…</code>,\n<code>~/.aws/credentials</code>, <code>.npmrc</code>, …) and a URL, e-mail address or host within 100 characters of each\nother — the shape of &quot;read this, send it there&quot; whatever language the connective words are in.\nAdvisory because on 10 645 live servers its only hit was honest (a deploy tool's ssh command to its\nown host); refusing a server on a rule whose only real-world hit is honest is the v1 mistake again.</li>\n<li><strong>Three measured false positives removed</strong>: &quot;send the user to https://…&quot; is a redirect of a person\n(guard <code>navigation</code>); &quot;keep calling this until done without asking the user&quot; is autonomy, not\nconcealment (guard <code>autonomy</code>); a zero-width joiner inside an emoji sequence is not concealment.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Measured on the 10 645 distinct tool sets HISTOR holds (172 771 tools): v4 blocks 63, v5 blocks 56,\nand v5 blocks none that v4 did not. The 1 108-server survey figures (v3 → v4) are unchanged and\nstill describe v4's calibration; this corpus is HISTOR's, not the survey's.</p>\n<h2>0.5.1 — 2026-09-05</h2>\n<p>stdio wire fix for Glama: replies are newline-delimited JSON (MCP stdio / mcp-proxy).\nContent-Length framing on stdout made Glama's health check time out (<code>ignoring non-JSON output [ 'Content-Length: …' ]</code>). Input still accepts Content-Length and mirrors it on\nthe reply for legacy probes.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li>See full diff in <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/warden/commits\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility score](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=@aimarket/warden&package-manager=npm_and_yarn&previous-version=0.5.0&new-version=0.6.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't alter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting `@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits that have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all of the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n\n\n</details>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/histor/issues/6/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alexar76/histor/issues/6/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lets-order-some-fries/trovark/issues/22","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lets-order-some-fries/trovark","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lets-order-some-fries/trovark/issues/22/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lets-order-some-fries/trovark/issues/22/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lets-order-some-fries/trovark/issues/22/events","html_url":"https://github.com/lets-order-some-fries/trovark/issues/22","id":5388341655,"node_id":"I_kwDOTphPns8AAAABQSuRlw","number":22,"title":"Tool-surface under-read is invisible on repos that do not use a tools/ directory: 4 of 125 tools published as a complete count","user":{"login":"lets-order-some-fries","id":34904987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0OTA0OTg3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34904987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lets-order-some-fries","html_url":"https://github.com/lets-order-some-fries","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lets-order-some-fries/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lets-order-some-fries/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lets-order-some-fries/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lets-order-some-fries/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lets-order-some-fries/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lets-order-some-fries/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lets-order-some-fries/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lets-order-some-fries/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lets-order-some-fries/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-09-08T14:58:49Z","updated_at":"2026-09-25T17:01:48Z","closed_at":"2026-09-25T17:01:48Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## What happens\n\n`github/github-mcp-server` — the repo used as the headline example in README.md:7 and as the\nsample `--json` scorecard at README.md:131-134 — is published with **`toolCount: 4`**.\n\nThe repo actually defines **125 distinct tool names**, 34 of them write or delete verbs\n(`delete_file`, `push_files`, `merge_pull_request`, `create_or_update_file`,\n`create_repository`, `fork_repository`, …).\n\nThe four that were read are `ui_get`, `get_me`, `get_teams`, `get_team_members` — all\nread-only, all from a 13-file sample. Everything downstream then treats that sample as the\nwhole surface:\n\n| field | published | reality |\n|---|---|---|\n| `toolCount` | 4 | 125 |\n| `toolSurfaceRisk` | `low` | 34 destructive verbs |\n| cost | 100/100 (the ≤10-tools band) | not measurable from 4 of 125 |\n| security | 85/100 (primary, weight 3 of 6) | built on the wrong risk |\n| overall | **96/100 A+** | — |\n| `errors` | `[]` | — |\n| partial-read note | none | — |\n\nThere is no signal anywhere on the card that the read was partial.\n\n## Why the existing guard misses it\n\n`isToolFanoutPath` (src/collectors/github.ts:293) only matches `(^|/)tools?/` or `.tools.ts`.\nThis repo keeps its 56 non-test tool files in `pkg/github/*.go`, so `toolFanoutCount` is `0`,\n`detectSurfacePartial` (src/derive/schema.ts:1411) evaluates `0 > 0` as false, `surfacePartial`\nstays false, and src/assemble.ts:226-228 publishes the sample count as complete.\n\nThe guard itself works — `grafana/mcp-grafana` keeps its tools under `tools/`, the guard fires,\nand cost is correctly withheld. The detector is coupled to one directory convention rather than\nto the thing it is trying to measure.\n\n## Suggested direction\n\nMake the partiality check independent of directory naming: after extraction, for each directory\nthat produced an extracted tool (`schema.tools[].evidence` already carries the source path),\ncompare how many source files that directory holds in the tree against how many were fetched.\nSampled < detected means `surfacePartial`.\n\n## Why this is filed rather than fixed\n\n**It moves published grades.** Servers currently graded would flip to withheld cost/security,\nand some to INSUFFICIENT DATA through the `securityPrimaryAbsent` gate in score.ts — including\nthe A+ 96 in the README. It is not a rubric change (no weights, bands or `RUBRIC_VERSION`\ntouched), but the blast radius should be measured against `index/results.json` before landing,\nand the README example probably needs choosing again afterwards.\n\nThat is a call for the maintainer, not something to slip in.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n```\nnode dist/assemble.js github/github-mcp-server\n# => {\"toolCount\":4,\"toolNames\":[\"ui_get\",\"get_me\",\"get_teams\",\"get_team_members\"],\n#     \"toolSurfaceRisk\":\"low\",\"schemaExtracted\":true,\"errors\":[]}\n```\n\nGround truth: grep for `Name: \"...\"` inside `mcp.Tool{}` literals under `pkg/github/*.go`.\n\nContrast: `grafana/mcp-grafana` in the same run returns `toolCount: undefined` with cost withheld.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lets-order-some-fries/trovark/issues/22/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lets-order-some-fries/trovark/issues/22/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/issues/28","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/issues/28/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/issues/28/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/issues/28/events","html_url":"https://github.com/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pull/28","id":4045880613,"node_id":"PR_kwDONvrgrc7JFo5u","number":28,"title":"Next.js 16 / React 19 メジャーアップグレードとコードベース監査・堅牢化計画 (Plan 001〜006) の策定","user":{"login":"myoshi2891","id":96483039,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcA23w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96483039?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myoshi2891","html_url":"https://github.com/myoshi2891","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myoshi2891/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myoshi2891/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myoshi2891/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myoshi2891/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myoshi2891/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myoshi2891/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myoshi2891/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myoshi2891/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myoshi2891/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":52,"created_at":"2026-03-09T14:18:35Z","updated_at":"2026-09-18T11:09:25Z","closed_at":"2026-09-18T11:09:24Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/28","html_url":"https://github.com/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pull/28","diff_url":"https://github.com/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pull/28.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pull/28.patch","merged_at":"2026-09-18T11:09:24Z"},"body":"大きく分けて以下の5つの柱で対応が進められました：\r\n\r\n1. **Next.js 16 / React 19 / Clerk v7 へのメジャー移行（TDDアプローチ）**\r\n2. **セキュリティ脆弱性（Image Optimizer DoS, AVIF RCE, SSRF等）へのパッチ対応**\r\n3. **型安全性・Lint・CIスクリプト等の開発基盤刷新**\r\n4. **AIエージェント向け監査・改善スキル（`improve` / `closing-the-loop`）の構築**\r\n5. **プロダクト堅牢化に向けた6つの詳細実装計画書（`plans/001〜006`）の策定・精緻化**\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## **主な対応内容**\r\n\r\n### **1. フレームワークのメジャーアップグレード & 互換性修正 (TDD)**\r\n\r\nテストを先行作成（RED）した上で、破壊的変更への移行を完了：\r\n\r\n- **React 19 移行**: 非推奨となった `useFormState` を  へ刷新。\r\n    \r\n    **`useActionState`**\r\n    \r\n- **Next.js 16 移行**: `params` / `searchParams` の非同期化（`Promise`）に対応し、関連ページやテストを改修。\r\n- **Clerk v7 移行**: `auth()` の呼び出しを `async/await` に移行。\r\n- **型安全性向上**: Server Actions の `prevState` を `any` から `{ message: string }` に型制約を厳格化。\r\n\r\n### **2. セキュリティ脆弱性対策とパッチ適用**\r\n\r\n- **Next.js の段階的バージョンアップ**: 16.2.11 → 16.3.3 へ更新し、既知の脆弱性（GHSA-9g9p-9gw9-jx7f, AVIF RCE: GHSA-2xp9-vwfh-vxw4）に対処。\r\n- **画像オプティマイザ防御**:  の `remotePatterns` に `pathname` 制限を追加し、Image Optimizer DoS（GHSA-q8wf-6r8g-63ch）および Clerk ホストのパスマッチを厳格化。\r\n    \r\n    **next.config.mjs**\r\n    \r\n- **SSRF & 入力検証**: チェックアウト時の入力バリデーションおよび SSRF 対策のための環境制限を導入。\r\n- **認可ロジック抽出**: `middleware.ts` から `isAdminUser` を独立した実関数として切り出し、単体テストを追加。\r\n\r\n### **3. ツールチェーン & 品質保証の改善**\r\n\r\n- **ESLint 9 Flat Config への移行**:  から  へ刷新。\r\n    \r\n    **.eslintrc.json**\r\n    \r\n    **eslint.config.mjs**\r\n    \r\n- **型検査コマンド新設**: `package.json` に `typecheck` スクリプトを追加し、`test` 実行時に型チェックを統合。\r\n- **リグレッション検証**: Checkout ページの `Suspense` boundary 内包確認、`searchParams` の配列入力対応やパラメータ正規化のテストを拡充。\r\n\r\n### **4. 改善スキル（`improve` / `closing-the-loop`）の設計・強化**\r\n\r\n**.agents/skills/improve/** 配下に、コードベース監査とタスク実行を自律化・安全化するための規約を定義：\r\n\r\n- **監査プレイブック & テンプレート**: `audit-playbook.md`, `plan-template.md` の標準化。\r\n- **安全規約・ドリフト検証**: 実行時のベースコミット (`execution base SHA`) に基づくスコープ検証、プロンプトインジェクション対策、STALE 状態ハンドリング、GitHub Issue 重複作成抑止ルールを整備。","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/issues/28/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/issues/28/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hyperpolymath/rsr-template-repo/issues/83","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hyperpolymath/rsr-template-repo","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hyperpolymath/rsr-template-repo/issues/83/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hyperpolymath/rsr-template-repo/issues/83/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hyperpolymath/rsr-template-repo/issues/83/events","html_url":"https://github.com/hyperpolymath/rsr-template-repo/pull/83","id":5412290100,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTeRBCM8AAAABC_fpiA","number":83,"title":"Exempt reviewed Hypatia research-extension findings","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":16,"created_at":"2026-09-10T12:40:41Z","updated_at":"2026-09-17T17:05:22Z","closed_at":"2026-09-17T17:05:21Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hyperpolymath/rsr-template-repo/pulls/83","html_url":"https://github.com/hyperpolymath/rsr-template-repo/pull/83","diff_url":"https://github.com/hyperpolymath/rsr-template-repo/pull/83.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/hyperpolymath/rsr-template-repo/pull/83.patch","merged_at":"2026-09-17T17:05:21Z"},"body":"Add narrowly scoped Hypatia ignore entries for reviewed RE001, RE005, and RE008 findings across affected workflows, documenting why each advisory does not apply while preserving checks for new workflows. This aligns with the task intent by preventing the known Hypatia scan failures. Validation was not run.\n\n[View coding task](https://app.coderabbit.ai/code/tasks/f36ac704-d4fb-467c-8b3e-1c03b4b82f62?source=coding_agent_github_pr_description)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hyperpolymath/rsr-template-repo/issues/83/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hyperpolymath/rsr-template-repo/issues/83/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e2b-dev/awesome-ai-sdks/issues/217","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e2b-dev/awesome-ai-sdks","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e2b-dev/awesome-ai-sdks/issues/217/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e2b-dev/awesome-ai-sdks/issues/217/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e2b-dev/awesome-ai-sdks/issues/217/events","html_url":"https://github.com/e2b-dev/awesome-ai-sdks/pull/217","id":4557932663,"node_id":"PR_kwDOKDzNHs7hGxLA","number":217,"title":"Add AIMarket Agent and AIMarket SDKs (protocol v2)","user":{"login":"alexart2025","id":203622159,"node_id":"U_kgDODCMHDw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203622159?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025","html_url":"https://github.com/alexart2025","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10897423376,"node_id":"LA_kwDOKDzNHs8AAAACiYl8EA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e2b-dev/awesome-ai-sdks/labels/cla-signed","name":"cla-signed","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-05-31T14:54:11Z","updated_at":"2026-07-29T19:37:46Z","closed_at":"2026-07-29T19:37:46Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e2b-dev/awesome-ai-sdks/pulls/217","html_url":"https://github.com/e2b-dev/awesome-ai-sdks/pull/217","diff_url":"https://github.com/e2b-dev/awesome-ai-sdks/pull/217.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/e2b-dev/awesome-ai-sdks/pull/217.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## Summary\nAdds two related SDKs for [AIMarket Protocol v2](https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-protocol) — federated discovery, HTTP 402 payment channels, safety-gated invoke, and settlement with signed receipts.\n\n| Project | Role |\n|---------|------|\n| [aimarket-agent](https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-agent) | Python SDK + CLI (`pip install aimarket-agent`) |\n| [aimarket-sdks](https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks) | Dart (alpha), TypeScript/Rust clients |\n\nReference hub: https://modelmarket.dev\n\n## Why this list\nThese are client libraries for building autonomous agents that discover and pay for capabilities across a federation — aligned with “SDKs for creating and deploying AI agents.”\n\nNot affiliated with e2b; independent open-source (MIT).","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e2b-dev/awesome-ai-sdks/issues/217/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e2b-dev/awesome-ai-sdks/issues/217/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/issues/8422","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/issues/8422/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/issues/8422/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/issues/8422/events","html_url":"https://github.com/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/pull/8422","id":4708230139,"node_id":"PR_kwDONWz9ps7owMul","number":8422,"title":"Add aimarket-oracle-gateway (verifiable oracle MCP server)","user":{"login":"alexart2025","id":203622159,"node_id":"U_kgDODCMHDw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203622159?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025","html_url":"https://github.com/alexart2025","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10350553194,"node_id":"LA_kwDONWz9ps8AAAACaPDoag","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/labels/has-emoji","name":"has-emoji","color":"40d01d","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":10350553200,"node_id":"LA_kwDONWz9ps8AAAACaPDocA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/labels/valid-name","name":"valid-name","color":"40d01d","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":10350561209,"node_id":"LA_kwDONWz9ps8AAAACaPEHuQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/labels/has-glama","name":"has-glama","color":"40d01d","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-06-20T20:12:08Z","updated_at":"2026-07-11T14:27:28Z","closed_at":"2026-07-11T14:27:18Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/pulls/8422","html_url":"https://github.com/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/pull/8422","diff_url":"https://github.com/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/pull/8422.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/pull/8422.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## Summary\n\nAdds **alexar76/aimarket-oracle-gateway** to the **Security** section — a separate MCP server from our existing **Aggregators** entry (`aimarket-plugins` / mcp-packager).\n\nMIT · Python · stdio MCP server exposing verifiable oracle tools for AI agents:\n- **Platon VRF** — Ed25519-signed unbiasable randomness (`get_random`, `get_randomness_beacon`, `ask_oracle`)\n- **Chronos VDF** — verifiable delay / proof-of-elapsed-time (`compute_vdf`, `verify_vdf`)\n- **LUMEN reputation** — PageRank/EigenTrust trust scores (`get_reputation_scores`)\n- `list_oracle_capabilities`\n\nPay-per-call over the [AIMarket Protocol v2](https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-protocol); every result is independently verifiable. Fail-closed spend caps.\n\n- Repo: https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-oracle-gateway\n- Glama: https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/alexar76/aimarket-oracle-gateway\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Alphabetical placement in Security (after `alexfleetcommander`, before `alberthild`)\n- [x] Distinct from existing `alexar76/aimarket-plugins` Aggregators entry (different repo, different purpose)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/issues/8422/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers/issues/8422/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}